acrifice an artifact: Target artifact gains indestructible until end of turn.', 'Sea of Clouds enters the battlefield tapped unless you have two or more opponents.\\n{T}: Add {W} or {U}.', "Search target opponent's library for an artifact, creature, enchantment, or land card. Put that card onto the battlefield under your control. Then that player shuffles.\\nEpic (For the rest of the game, you can't cast spells. At the beginning of each of your upkeeps, copy this spell except for its epic ability. You may choose a new target for the copy.)", 'Search your library and graveyard for five cards and exile the rest. Put the chosen cards on top of your library in any order. You lose half your life, rounded up.', 'Search your library for a basic land card, put it onto the battlefield, then shuffle. (Then exile this card. You may cast the creature later from exile.)', 'Search your library for a card, put that card into your hand, then shuffle.', 'Search your library for a card, then shuffle and put that card on top. You lose 2 life.', 'Search your library for a snow land card, put it onto the battlefield tapped, then shuffle.', 'Search your library for an artifact card, reveal it, put it into your hand, then shuffle.', 'Search your library for an artifact or enchantment card, reveal it, then shuffle and put that card on top.', 'Search your library for an instant or sorcery card, reveal it, then shuffle and put that card on top.', 'Search your library for up to X basic land cards, where X is the greatest power among creatures you control. Put those cards onto the battlefield tapped, then shuffle.', "Separate all creature cards in your graveyard into two piles. Exile the pile of an opponent's choice and return the other to the battlefield.", 'Shivan Meteor deals 13 damage to target creature.\\nSuspend 2—{1}{R}{R} (Rather than cast this card from your hand, you may pay {1}{R}{R} and exile it with two time counters on it. At the beginning of your upkeep, remove a time counter. When the last is removed, cast it without paying its mana cost.)', "Shroud (This enchantment can't be the target of spells or abilities.)\\n{X}: Put X tower counters on Helix Pinnacle.\\nAt the beginning of your upkeep, if there are 100 or more tower counters on Helix Pinnacle, you win the game.", "Shuffle your library, then reveal the top card. If it's a nonland card, you may cast it without paying its mana cost. If it's a land card, you may put it onto the battlefield and return Unexpected Results to its owner's hand.", 'Skred deals damage to target creature equal to the number of snow permanents you control.', "Slag Fiend's power and toughness are each equal to the number of artifact cards in all graveyards.", "Sorin's Vengeance deals 10 damage to target player or planeswalker and you gain 10 life.", 'Soulbond (You may pair this creature with another unpaired creature when either enters the battlefield. They remain paired for as long as you control both of them.)\\nAs long as Nightshade Peddler is paired with another creature, both creatures have deathtouch.', 'Soulbond (You may pair this creature with another unpaired creature when either enters the battlefield. They remain paired for as long as you control both of them.)\\nAs long as Wolfir Silverheart is paired with another creature, each of those creatures gets +4/+4.', 'Spectacle {R} (You may cast this spell for its spectacle cost rather than its mana cost if an opponent lost life this turn.)\\nExile the top two cards of your library. Until the end of your next turn, you may play those cards.', "Spells and abilities your opponents control can't cause you to discard cards or sacrifice permanents.\\n[+1]: Choose a nonland card name, then reveal the top four cards of your library. Put all cards with the chosen name from among them into your hand and the rest into your graveyard.\\n[−3]: Return target card from your graveyard to your hand.", 'Spells you cast have ripple 4. (Whenever you cast a spell, you may reveal the top four cards of your library. You may cast spells with the same name as that spell from among the revealed cards without paying their mana costs. Put the rest on the bottom of your library.)', 'Spells your opponents cast that target a creature or planeswalker you control cost {2} more to cast.\\n[−2]: Create a 2/2 blue Wizard creature token. Draw a card, then discard a card.', 'Spike Weaver enters the battlefield with three +1/+1 counters on it.\\n{2}, Remove a +1/+1 counter from Spike Weaver: Put a +1/+1 counter on target creature.\\n{1}, Remove a +1/+1 counter from Spike Weaver: Prevent all combat damage that would be dealt this turn.', "Split second (As long as this spell is on the stack, players can't cast spells or activate abilities that aren't mana abilities.)\\nYou can't lose the game this turn and your opponents can't win the game this turn. Until end of turn, damage that would reduce your life total to less than 1 reduces it to 1 instead.", 'Squirrel Mob gets +1/+1 for each other Squirrel on the battlefield.', 'Sunburst (This enters the battlefield with a +1/+1 counter on it for each color of mana spent to cast it.)\\nRemove a +1/+1 counter from Lunar Avenger: Lunar Avenger gains your choice of flying, first strike, or haste until end of turn.', 'Sunburst (This enters the battlefield with a charge counter on it for each color of mana spent to cast it.)\\nAt the beginning of your upkeep, you may gain life equal to the number of charge counters on Clearwater Goblet.', 'Surge {X}{R} (You may cast this spell for its surge cost if you or a teammate has cast another spell this turn.)\\nFall of the Titans deals X damage to each of up to two targets.', 'Suspend 3—{0} (Rather than cast this card from your hand, pay {0} and exile it with three time counters on it. At the beginning of your upkeep, remove a time counter. When the last is removed, cast it without paying its mana cost.)\\n{T}, Sacrifice Lotus Bloom: Add three mana of any one color.', 'Suspend 4—{G}\\nUntil end of turn, you may play lands and cast spells from your graveyard.\\nIf a card would be put into your graveyard from anywhere this turn, exile that card instead.', "Swampwalk (This creature can't be blocked as long as defending player controls a Swamp.)\\nAt the beginning of your upkeep, return target creature card from your graveyard to the battlefield.\\nAt the beginning of each opponent's upkeep, that player sacrifices a creature.", "Swampwalk (This creature can't be blocked as long as defending player controls a Swamp.)\\n{T}: Add {B}{B}{B}{B}. Target opponent gains control of Witch Engine. (Activate only as an instant.)", "Sweep — Return any number of Swamps you control to their owner's hand. Target player discards a card for each Swamp returned this way.", 'Take an extra turn after this one.', "Tap all creatures target player controls. Those creatures don't untap during that player's next untap step.", 'Tap an untapped Cephalid you control: Tap target permanent.\\n{U}{U}{U}: Tap all creatures without flying.', 'Tap an untapped Wizard you control: Counter target spell unless its controller pays {1}.', 'Tap five untapped Clerics you control: You gain 10 life.', 'Tap five untapped Zombies you control: Put target creature card from a graveyard onto the battlefield under your control.', 'Tap three untapped creatures you control: Each opponent loses 1 life.', 'Target creature attacks this turn if able.\\nDraw a card.', 'Target creature gains flying until end of turn.', 'Target creature gets -1/-1 until end of turn.', 'Target creature gets -1/-1 until end of turn. Scry 2. (Look at the top two cards of your library, then put any number of them on the bottom of your library and the rest on top in any order.)', 'Target creature you control deals damage equal to its power to any target.\\nFuse (You may cast one or both halves of this card from your hand.)', 'Target opponent loses 5 life unless that player discards two cards or sacrifices a creature or planeswalker. Repeat this process once.', "Target player can't play lands this turn if {R} was spent to cast this spell and can't cast creature spells this turn if {W} was spent to cast this spell. (Do both if {R}{W} was spent.)", 'Target player discards two cards at random.', 'Target player discards two cards. That player may copy this spell and may choose a new target for that copy.', 'Target player draws four cards.', 'Target player draws two cards and loses 2 life.', 'Target player mills three cards.\\nStorm (When you cast this spell, copy it for each spell cast before it this turn. You may choose new targets for the copies.)', 'Target player sacrifices a creature and loses 1 life.', 'Target player sacrifices two attacking creatures.', 'Target player takes two extra turns after this one.', 'Target player untaps all basic lands they control.', 'Target spell or permanent becomes colorless.', 'Target spell or permanent becomes the color of your choice until end of turn.', "Tarmogoyf's power is equal to the number of card types among cards in all graveyards and its toughness is equal to that number plus 1.", 'Tek gets +0/+2 as long as you control a Plains, has flying as long as you control an Island, gets +2/+0 as long as you control a Swamp, has first strike as long as you control a Mountain, and has trample as long as you control a Forest.', 'Tendo Ice Bridge enters the battlefield with a charge counter on it.\\n{T}: Add {C}.\\n{T}, Remove a charge counter from Tendo Ice Bridge: Add one mana of any color.', 'The "legend rule" doesn\'t apply.', 'The World Tree enters the battlefield tapped.\\n{T}: Add {G}.\\nAs long as you control six or more lands, lands you control have "{T}: Add one mana of any color."\\n{W}{W}{U}{U}{B}{B}{R}{R}{G}{G}, {T}, Sacrifice The World Tree: Search your library for any number of God cards, put them onto the battlefield, then shuffle.', 'The first spell you cast each turn has cascade. (When you cast your first spell, exile cards from the top of your library until you exile a nonland card that costs less. You may cast it without paying its mana cost. Put the exiled cards on the bottom of your library in a random order.)', "This spell can't be countered.\\nDestroy all artifacts, creatures, and lands. They can't be regenerated.", "This spell can't be countered.\\nDestroy target nonland permanent with mana value 3 or less.", "This spell can't be countered.\\nFlying, lifelink\\nYour opponents can't cast spells during your turn.", "This spell can't be countered.\\nHaste\\nGaea's Revenge can't be the target of nongreen spells or abilities from nongreen sources.", "This spell can't be countered.\\nMagic Missile deals 3 damage divided as you choose among one, two, or three targets.", "This spell can't be countered.\\nWhen you cast this spell, take an extra turn after this one.\\nFlying, protection from spells that are one or more colors, annihilator 6\\nWhen Emrakul, the Aeons Torn is put into a graveyard from anywhere, its owner shuffles their graveyard into their library.", 'This spell costs {1} less to cast for each creature card in your graveyard.\\nDuring each of your turns, you may cast a creature spell from your graveyard.', 'This spell costs {1} less to cast for each creature in your party. (Your party consists of up to one each of Cleric, Rogue, Warrior, and Wizard.)\\nYou gain 3 life and draw three cards.', 'This spell costs {1} less to cast if you control a Wizard.\\nCounter target spell.', 'This spell costs {1} more to cast for each target beyond the first.\\nFireball deals X damage divided evenly, rounded down, among any number of targets.', 'This spell costs {G} less to cast for each green creature you control.\\nTrample', 'This spell costs {X} less to cast, where X is the total power of creatures you control.\\nTrample', 'Threshold — As long as seven or more cards are in your graveyard, Treacherous Werewolf gets +2/+2 and has "When Treacherous Werewolf dies, you lose 4 life."', 'Toxic Iguanar has deathtouch as long as you control a green permanent. (Any amount of damage a creature with deathtouch deals to a creature is enough to destroy it.)', "Training Drone can't attack or block unless it's equipped.", 'Trample', "Trample (This creature can deal excess combat damage to the player or planeswalker it's attacking.)\\nColossus of Sardia doesn't untap during your untap step.\\n{9}: Untap Colossus of Sardia. Activate only during your upkeep.", "Trample (This creature can deal excess combat damage to the player or planeswalker it's attacking.)\\nWhen Crumbling Colossus attacks, sacrifice it at end of combat.", 'Trample, haste\\nAt the beginning of the end step, sacrifice Groundbreaker.', "Trample, infect, indestructible\\nIf Blightsteel Colossus would be put into a graveyard from anywhere, reveal Blightsteel Colossus and shuffle it into its owner's library instead.", 'Trample\\nAt the beginning of your upkeep, sacrifice Endless Wurm unless you sacrifice an enchantment.', 'Trample\\nEcho {1}{G}{G} (At the beginning of your upkeep, if this came under your control since the beginning of your last upkeep, sacrifice it unless you pay its echo cost.)', "Trample\\nJokulmorder enters the battlefield tapped.\\nWhen Jokulmorder enters the battlefield, sacrifice it unless you sacrifice five lands.\\nJokulmorder doesn't untap during your untap step.\\nWhenever you play an Island, you may untap Jokulmorder.", 'Trample\\nKalonian Hydra enters the battlefield with four +1/+1 counters on it.\\nWhenever Kalonian Hydra attacks, double the number of +1/+1 counters on each creature you control.', 'Trample\\nWhen Fierce Witchstalker enters the battlefield, create a Food token. (It\'s an artifact with "{2}, {T}, Sacrifice this artifact: You gain 3 life.")', 'Trample\\nWhen Verdurous Gearhulk enters the battlefield, distribute four +1/+1 counters among any number of target creatures you control.', 'Trample\\nWhenever Borborygmos Enraged deals combat damage to a player, reveal the top three cards of your library. Put all land cards revealed this way into your hand and the rest into your graveyard.\\nDiscard a land card: Borborygmos Enraged deals 3 damage to any target.', "Trample\\nWhenever Spectral Force attacks, if defending player controls no black permanents, it doesn't untap during your next untap step.", "Trample\\nWhenever a source deals damage to Phyrexian Obliterator, that source's controller sacrifices that many permanents.", 'Trample\\nWhenever you cast a noncreature spell, Mizzium Tank becomes an artifact creature and gets +1/+1 until end of turn.\\nCrew 1 (Tap any number of creatures you control with total power 1 or more: This Vehicle becomes an artifact creature until end of turn.)', "Trample\\nWhenever you tap a land for mana, add one mana of any type that land produced.\\nWhenever an opponent taps a land for mana, that land doesn't untap during its controller's next untap step.", "Trample\\nWhile you're searching your library, you may cast Panglacial Wurm from your library.", 'Trample\\n{5}: Permanents you control gain indestructible until end of turn.\\n{5}, Exile Soul of New Phyrexia from your graveyard: Permanents you control gain indestructible until end of turn.', 'Trample\\n{G}: Regenerate Silvos, Rogue Elemental.', 'Transform all Humans. Prevent all combat damage that would be dealt this turn by creatures other than Werewolves and Wolves. (Only double-faced cards can be transformed.)', 'Transmogrifying Wand enters the battlefield with three charge counters on it.\\n{1}, {T}, Remove a charge counter from Transmogrifying Wand: Destroy target creature. Its controller creates a 2/4 white Ox creature token. Activate only as a sorcery.', "Tymaret's toughness is equal to your devotion to black. (Each {B} in the mana costs of permanents you control counts toward your devotion to black.)\\n{1}{B}: Exile up to two target cards from graveyards. You gain 1 life for each creature card exiled this way.", "Untap all artifacts you control during each other player's untap step.", 'Until end of turn, creatures you control gain protection from white if you control a Plains, from blue if you control an Island, from black if you control a Swamp, from red if you control a Mountain, and from green if you control a Forest.', 'Until end of turn, up to two target creatures you control each gain "Whenever this creature deals combat damage to a player, draw a card."', 'Vampiric Feast deals 4 damage to any target and you gain 4 life.', 'Vigilance', 'Vigilance, lifelink\\n{T}: Create a 4/4 white Angel creature token with flying. Activate only if you have at least 7 life more than your starting life total and only as a sorcery.', 'Vigilance, reach, trample\\nWhen Zacama, Primal Calamity enters the battlefield, if you cast it, untap all lands you control.\\n{2}{R}: Zacama deals 3 damage to target creature.\\n{2}{G}: Destroy target artifact or enchantment.\\n{2}{W}: You gain 3 life.', "Vigilance, trample\\n{2}, {T}: Exile another target creature. Return that card to the battlefield under its owner's control at the beginning of the next end step.", 'Vigilance\\nHeroic — Whenever you cast a spell that targets Vanguard of Brimaz, create a 1/1 white Cat Soldier creature token with vigilance.', 'Vigilance\\nInfect (This creature deals damage to creatures in the form of -1/-1 counters and to players in the form of poison counters.)', "Vigilance\\nKemba's Legion can block an additional creature each combat for each Equipment attached to Kemba's Legion.", 'Vigilance\\nLieutenant — At the beginning of combat on your turn, if you control your commander, prevent all combat damage that would be dealt to creatures you control this turn. Other creatures you control gain vigilance until end of turn.', 'Vigilance\\nWhenever Sun Titan enters the battlefield or attacks, you may return target permanent card with mana value 3 or less from your graveyard to the battlefield.', 'Vigilance\\nWhenever a white creature you control attacks, you gain 1 life.', "Vigilance\\nWhenever you cast a creature spell, draw a card, then you may put a land card from your hand onto the battlefield.\\n{3}, {T}: Return target creature you control to its owner's hand.", 'Vigilance\\n{1}{W}, {T}: Search your library for an Equipment card, put it onto the battlefield, attach it to a creature you control, then shuffle.', 'Vigilance\\n{2}: Add one mana of any color.', "Vigilance\\n{3}{W}{W}{W}: Monstrosity 3. (If this creature isn't monstrous, put three +1/+1 counters on it and it becomes monstrous.)\\nAs long as Hundred-Handed One is monstrous, it has reach and can block an additional ninety-nine creatures each combat.", "Vigilance\\n{T}: Create an 8/8 Beast creature token that's red, green, and white.", 'Vigilance\\n{T}: Untap target attacking creature. Prevent all combat damage that would be dealt to and dealt by that creature this turn.\\nSuspend 4—{W}{U}', "Vintara Snapper has shroud as long as you control no untapped lands. (It can't be the target of spells or abilities.)", "When Archaeomancer's Map enters the battlefield, search your library for up to two basic Plains cards, reveal them, put them into your hand, then shuffle.\\nWhenever a land enters the battlefield under an opponent's control, if that player controls more lands than you, you may put a land card from your hand onto the battlefield.", "When Architects of Will enters the battlefield, look at the top three cards of target player's library, then put them back in any order.\\nCycling {U/B} ({U/B}, Discard this card: Draw a card.)", 'When Avenger of Zendikar enters the battlefield, create a 0/1 green Plant creature token for each land you control.\\nLandfall — Whenever a land enters the battlefield under your control, you may put a +1/+1 counter on each Plant creature you control.', 'When Bane of Progress enters the battlefield, destroy all artifacts and enchantments. Put a +1/+1 counter on Bane of Progress for each permanent destroyed this way.', 'When Body Snatcher enters the battlefield, exile it unless you discard a creature card.\\nWhen Body Snatcher dies, exile Body Snatcher and return target creature card from your graveyard to the battlefield.', "When Brinelin, the Moon Kraken enters the battlefield or whenever you cast a spell with mana value 6 or greater, you may return target nonland permanent to its owner's hand.\\nPartner (You can have two commanders if both have partner.)", 'When Ceremonial Guard attacks or blocks, destroy it at end of combat.', "When Cloister Gargoyle enters the battlefield, venture into the dungeon. (Enter the first room or advance to the next room.)\\nAs long as you've completed a dungeon, Cloister Gargoyle gets +3/+0 and has flying.", 'When Cloudgoat Ranger enters the battlefield, create three 1/1 white Kithkin Soldier creature tokens.\\nTap three untapped Kithkin you control: Cloudgoat Ranger gets +2/+0 and gains flying until end of turn.', 'When Contagion Engine enters the battlefield, put a -1/-1 counter on each creature target player controls.\\n{4}, {T}: Proliferate, then proliferate again. (Choose any number of permanents and/or players, then give each another counter of each kind already there. Then do it again.)', "When Coveted Jewel enters the battlefield, draw three cards.\\n{T}: Add three mana of any one color.\\nWhenever one or more creatures an opponent controls attack you and aren't blocked, that player draws three cards and gains control of Coveted Jewel. Untap it.", "When Dispersal Technician enters the battlefield, you may return target artifact to its owner's hand.", "When Dromar's Cavern enters the battlefield, sacrifice it unless you return a non-Lair land you control to its owner's hand.\\n{T}: Add {W}, {U}, or {B}.", 'When Electrostatic Pummeler enters the battlefield, you get {E}{E}{E} (three energy counters).\\nPay {E}{E}{E}: Electrostatic Pummeler gets +X/+X until end of turn, where X is its power.', 'When Eternal Witness enters the battlefield, you may return target card from your graveyard to your hand.', 'When Gisa and Geralf enters the battlefield, mill four cards.\\nOnce during each of your turns, you may cast a Zombie creature spell from your graveyard.', 'When Golgari Thug dies, put target creature card from your graveyard on top of your library.\\nDredge 4 (If you would draw a card, you may mill four cards instead. If you do, return this card from your graveyard to your hand.)', "When Haru-Onna enters the battlefield, draw a card.\\nWhenever you cast a Spirit or Arcane spell, you may return Haru-Onna to its owner's hand.", 'When Hunted Troll enters the battlefield, target opponent creates four 1/1 blue Faerie creature tokens with flying.\\n{G}: Regenerate Hunted Troll.', "When Ixalan's Binding enters the battlefield, exile target nonland permanent an opponent controls until Ixalan's Binding leaves the battlefield.\\nYour opponents can't cast spells with the same name as the exiled card.", "When Jadelight Ranger enters the battlefield, it explores, then it explores again. (Reveal the top card of your library. Put that card into your hand if it's a land. Otherwise, put a +1/+1 counter on this creature, then put the card back or put it into your graveyard. Then repeat this process.)", "When Lazav, the Multifarious enters the battlefield, surveil 1. (Look at the top card of your library. You may put it into your graveyard.)\\n{X}: Lazav, the Multifarious becomes a copy of target creature card in your graveyard with mana value X, except its name is Lazav, the Multifarious, it's legendary in addition to its other types, and it has this ability.", "When Llawan, Cephalid Empress enters the battlefield, return all blue creatures your opponents control to their owners' hands.\\nYour opponents can't cast blue creature spells.", "When Man-o'-War enters the battlefield, return target creature to its owner's hand.", 'When Mindslicer dies, each player discards their hand.', 'When Minsc, Beloved Ranger enters the battlefield, create Boo, a legendary 1/1 red Hamster creature token with trample and haste.\\n{X}: Until end of turn, target creature you control has base power and toughness X/X and becomes a Giant in addition to its other types. Activate only as a sorcery.', 'When Mongrel Pack dies during combat, create four 1/1 green Dog creature tokens.', "When Murderous Redcap enters the battlefield, it deals damage equal to its power to any target.\\nPersist (When this creature dies, if it had no -1/-1 counters on it, return it to the battlefield under its owner's control with a -1/-1 counter on it.)", 'When Noble Benefactor dies, each player may search their library for a card and put that card into their hand. Then each player who searched their library this way shuffles.', 'When Noggle Hedge-Mage enters the battlefield, if you control two or more Islands, you may tap two target permanents.\\nWhen Noggle Hedge-Mage enters the battlefield, if you control two or more Mountains, you may have Noggle Hedge-Mage deal 2 damage to target player or planeswalker.', 'When Noxious Toad dies, each opponent discards a card.', 'When Opal Lake Gatekeepers enters the battlefield, if you control two or more Gates, you may draw a card.', "When Oubliette enters the battlefield, target creature phases out until Oubliette leaves the battlefield. Tap that creature as it phases in this way. (Auras and Equipment phase out with it. While permanents are phased out, they're treated as though they don't exist.)", 'When Path to the World Tree enters the battlefield, search your library for a basic land card, reveal it, put it into your hand, then shuffle.\\n{2}{W}{U}{B}{R}{G}, Sacrifice Path to the World Tree: You gain 2 life and draw two cards. Target opponent loses 2 life. Path to the World Tree deals 2 damage to up to one target creature. You create a 2/2 green Bear creature token.', "When Phyrexian Delver enters the battlefield, return target creature card from your graveyard to the battlefield. You lose life equal to that card's mana value.", 'When Phyrexian Triniform dies, create three 3/3 colorless Phyrexian Golem artifact creature tokens.\\nEncore {12} ({12}, Exile this card from your graveyard: For each opponent, create a token copy that attacks that opponent this turn if able. They gain haste. Sacrifice them at the beginning of the next end step. Activate only as a sorcery.)', 'When Pia and Kiran Nalaar enters the battlefield, create two 1/1 colorless Thopter artifact creature tokens with flying.\\n{2}{R}, Sacrifice an artifact: Pia and Kiran Nalaar deals 2 damage to any target.', 'When Pillaging Horde enters the battlefield, sacrifice it unless you discard a card at random.', 'When Priest of Gix enters the battlefield, add {B}{B}{B}.', 'When Ranger of Eos enters the battlefield, you may search your library for up to two creature cards with mana value 1 or less, reveal them, put them into your hand, then shuffle.', 'When Reclamation Sage enters the battlefield, you may destroy target artifact or enchantment.', 'When Rest in Peace enters the battlefield, exile all graveyards.\\nIf a card or token would be put into a graveyard from anywhere, exile it instead.', 'When Riftsweeper enters the battlefield, choose target face-up exiled card. Its owner shuffles it into their library.', 'When Sea Gate Oracle enters the battlefield, look at the top two cards of your library. Put one of them into your hand and the other on the bottom of your library.', "When Search the City enters the battlefield, exile the top five cards of your library.\\nWhenever you play a card with the same name as one of the exiled cards, you may put one of those cards with that name into its owner's hand. Then if there are no cards exiled with Search the City, sacrifice it. If you do, take an extra turn after this one.", 'When Sleeper Agent enters the battlefield, target opponent gains control of it.\\nAt the beginning of your upkeep, Sleeper Agent deals 2 damage to you.', "When Stitcher's Supplier enters the battlefield or dies, mill three cards.", 'When Tempting Wurm enters the battlefield, each opponent may put any number of artifact, creature, enchantment, and/or land cards from their hand onto the battlefield.', "When Thalia's Lieutenant enters the battlefield, put a +1/+1 counter on each other Human you control.\\nWhenever another Human enters the battlefield under your control, put a +1/+1 counter on Thalia's Lieutenant.", 'When Thundering Sparkmage enters the battlefield, it deals X damage to target creature or planeswalker, where X is the number of creatures in your party. (Your party consists of up to one each of Cleric, Rogue, Warrior, and Wizard.)', 'When Titania, Protector of Argoth enters the battlefield, return target land card from your graveyard to the battlefield.\\nWhenever a land you control is put into a graveyard from the battlefield, create a 5/3 green Elemental creature token.', 'When Treasure Hunter enters the battlefield, you may return target artifact card from your graveyard to your hand.', 'When Uro enters the battlefield, sacrifice it unless it escaped.\\nWhenever Uro enters the battlefield or attacks, you gain 3 life and draw a card, then you may put a land card from your hand onto the battlefield.\\nEscape—{G}{G}{U}{U}, Exile five other cards from your graveyard. (You may cast this card from your graveyard for its escape cost.)', 'When Venerated Teacher enters the battlefield, put two level counters on each creature you control with level up.', 'When Veteran Motorist enters the battlefield, scry 2.\\nWhenever Veteran Motorist crews a Vehicle, that Vehicle gets +1/+1 until end of turn.', 'When Whirlpool Warrior enters the battlefield, shuffle the cards from your hand into your library, then draw that many cards.\\n{R}, Sacrifice Whirlpool Warrior: Each player shuffles the cards from their hand into their library, then draws that many cards.', 'When Zhalfirin Void enters the battlefield, scry 1. (Look at the top card of your library. You may put that card on the bottom of your library.)\\n{T}: Add {C}.', 'When you cast this spell, any player may pay 5 life. If a player does, counter Dash Hopes.\\nCounter target spell.', 'When you cast this spell, create X 0/1 red Kobold creature tokens named Kobolds of Kher Keep, where X is the amount of mana spent to cast it.\\nFlying\\nSacrifice another creature: Prossh, Skyraider of Kher gets +1/+0 until end of turn.', 'When you cast this spell, draw four cards.\\nAnnihilator 4 (Whenever this creature attacks, defending player sacrifices four permanents.)\\nWhen Kozilek, Butcher of Truth is put into a graveyard from anywhere, its owner shuffles their graveyard into their library.', 'When you cast this spell, reveal the top X cards of your library. You may put a nonland permanent card with mana value X or less from among them onto the battlefield. Then shuffle the rest into your library.\\nGenesis Hydra enters the battlefield with X +1/+1 counters on it.', 'When you have 30 or more life, flip Rune-Tail, Kitsune Ascendant.', 'Whenever Arcbound Slith deals combat damage to a player, put a +1/+1 counter on it.\\nModular 1 (This creature enters the battlefield with a +1/+1 counter on it. When it dies, you may put its +1/+1 counters on target artifact creature.)', "Whenever Bonecrusher Giant becomes the target of a spell, Bonecrusher Giant deals 2 damage to that spell's controller.", 'Whenever Cruel Celebrant or another creature or planeswalker you control dies, each opponent loses 1 life and you gain 1 life.', 'Whenever Dune-Brood Nephilim deals combat damage to a player, create a 1/1 colorless Sand creature token for each land you control.', "Whenever Etali, Primal Storm attacks, exile the top card of each player's library, then you may cast any number of spells from among those cards without paying their mana costs.", "Whenever Exuberant Wolfbear attacks, you may change the base power and toughness of target Human you control to Exuberant Wolfbear's power and toughness until end of turn.", "Whenever Frost Titan becomes the target of a spell or ability an opponent controls, counter that spell or ability unless its controller pays {2}.\\nWhenever Frost Titan enters the battlefield or attacks, tap target permanent. It doesn't untap during its controller's next untap step.", 'Whenever Goblin Assassin or another Goblin enters the battlefield, each player flips a coin. Each player whose coin comes up tails sacrifices a creature.', "Whenever Hans Eriksson attacks, reveal the top card of your library. If it's a creature card, put it onto the battlefield tapped and attacking defending player or a planeswalker they control. Otherwise, put that card into your hand. When you put a creature card onto the battlefield this way, it fights Hans Eriksson.", 'Whenever Kalastria Highborn or another Vampire you control dies, you may pay {B}. If you do, target player loses 2 life and you gain 2 life.', "Whenever Krenko, Tin Street Kingpin attacks, put a +1/+1 counter on it, then create a number of 1/1 red Goblin creature tokens equal to Krenko's power.", "Whenever Krydle of Baldur's Gate deals combat damage to a player, that player loses 1 life and mills a card, then you gain 1 life and scry 1.\\nWhenever you attack, you may pay {2}. If you do, target creature can't be blocked this turn.", 'Whenever Lesser Gargadon attacks or blocks, sacrifice a land.', "Whenever Lorthos, the Tidemaker attacks, you may pay {8}. If you do, tap up to eight target permanents. Those permanents don't untap during their controllers' next untap steps.", 'Whenever Noxious Ghoul or another Zombie enters the battlefield, all non-Zombie creatures get -1/-1 until end of turn.', "Whenever Risen Reef or another Elemental enters the battlefield under your control, look at the top card of your library. If it's a land card, you may put it onto the battlefield tapped. If you don't put the card onto the battlefield, put it into your hand.", 'Whenever Saber Ants is dealt damage, you may create that many 1/1 green Insect creature tokens.', 'Whenever Sabertooth Cobra deals damage to a player, that player gets a poison counter. The player gets another poison counter at the beginning of their next upkeep unless they pay {2} before that step. (A player with ten or more poison counters loses the game.)', 'Whenever Stone Haven Pilgrim attacks, if you control an artifact or enchantment, Stone Haven Pilgrim gets +1/+1 and gains lifelink until end of turn.', 'Whenever Stonybrook Schoolmaster becomes tapped, you may create a 1/1 blue Merfolk Wizard creature token.', "Whenever Warchanter Skald becomes tapped, if it's enchanted or equipped, create a 2/1 red Dwarf Berserker creature token.", 'Whenever Yore-Tiller Nephilim attacks, return target creature card from your graveyard to the battlefield tapped and attacking.', "Whenever a Bird is put into your graveyard from the battlefield, put a feather counter on Soulcatchers' Aerie.\\nBird creatures get +1/+1 for each feather counter on Soulcatchers' Aerie.", 'Whenever a Saproling you control dies, Slimefoot, the Stowaway deals 1 damage to each opponent and you gain 1 life.\\n{4}: Create a 1/1 green Saproling creature token.', 'Whenever a creature attacks or blocks, Powerstone Minefield deals 2 damage to it.', 'Whenever a creature enters the battlefield this turn, you may draw a card.\\nFuse (You may cast one or both halves of this card from your hand.)', 'Whenever a creature enters the battlefield under your control, it gets +2/+0 and gains haste until end of turn.', 'Whenever a creature enters the battlefield under your control, you may destroy target artifact or enchantment.', "Whenever a creature enters the battlefield, that creature's controller may have it deal damage equal to its power to any target of their choice.", "Whenever a creature or planeswalker you control dies, you may sacrifice Ajani's Last Stand. If you do, create a 4/4 white Avatar creature token with flying.\\nWhen a spell or ability an opponent controls causes you to discard this card, if you control a Plains, create a 4/4 white Avatar creature token with flying.", "Whenever a creature token enters the battlefield under your control, you gain 1 life.\\nEmbalm {3}{W} ({3}{W}, Exile this card from your graveyard: Create a token that's a copy of it, except it's a white Zombie Human Cleric with no mana cost. Embalm only as a sorcery.)", 'Whenever a creature with power 2 or less enters the battlefield under your control, you get an experience counter.\\nAt the beginning of combat on your turn, put X +1/+1 counters on another target creature you control, where X is the number of experience counters you have.', "Whenever a creature you control attacks, it phases out at end of combat. (While it's phased out, it's treated as though it doesn't exist. It phases in before you untap during your next untap step.)", 'Whenever a creature you control deals combat damage, put a blaze counter on Five-Alarm Fire.\\nRemove five blaze counters from Five-Alarm Fire: It deals 5 damage to any target.', 'Whenever a creature you control dies, put a loyalty counter on Lolth, Spider Queen.\\n[0]: You draw a card and you lose 1 life.\\n[−3]: Create two 2/1 black Spider creature tokens with menace and reach.\\n[−8]: You get an emblem with "Whenever an opponent is dealt combat damage by one or more creatures you control, if that player lost less than 8 life this turn, they lose life equal to the difference."', 'Whenever a creature you control dies, you gain 1 life and draw a card.', "Whenever a creature you control that's enchanted or equipped attacks, that creature gains double strike until end of turn.", 'Whenever a land card is put into your graveyard from your library, you may pay {1}. If you do, draw a card.', "Whenever a nontoken creature is put into your graveyard from the battlefield, if Bridge from Below is in your graveyard, create a 2/2 black Zombie creature token.\\nWhen a creature is put into an opponent's graveyard from the battlefield, if Bridge from Below is in your graveyard, exile Bridge from Below.", 'Whenever a nontoken creature you control dies, investigate. (Create a Clue token. It\'s an artifact with "{2}, Sacrifice this artifact: Draw a card.")\\nWhenever you sacrifice a Clue, create a 1/1 white Human Soldier creature token.', 'Whenever a nontoken creature you control dies, put a slime counter on Gutter Grime, then create a green Ooze creature token with "This creature\'s power and toughness are each equal to the number of slime counters on Gutter Grime."', "Whenever a nontoken creature you control dies, you gain 1 life. Then you may draw a card. If you do, discard a card.\\n{2}, {T}, Sacrifice Gate to the Afterlife: Search your graveyard, hand, and/or library for a card named God-Pharaoh's Gift and put it onto the battlefield. If you search your library this way, shuffle. Activate only if there are six or more creature cards in your graveyard.", 'Whenever a permanent an opponent controls is put into a graveyard from the battlefield, put a +1/+1 counter on Sarulf, Realm Eater.\\nAt the beginning of your upkeep, if Sarulf has one or more +1/+1 counters on it, you may remove all of them. If you do, exile each other nonland permanent with mana value less than or equal to the number of counters removed this way.', 'Whenever a permanent you control transforms into a non-Human creature, create a 2/2 green Wolf creature token.', "Whenever a player casts a noncreature spell, each of that player's opponents may draw a card.", 'Whenever a player casts a spell with mana value 3 or less, Eidolon of the Great Revel deals 2 damage to that player.', "Whenever a player casts a spell, any other player may pay that spell's mana cost. If a player does, counter the spell. (Mana cost includes color.)", 'Whenever a player casts an artifact spell, you may gain 1 life.', 'Whenever a player casts an instant or sorcery card, exile it. Then that player copies each instant or sorcery card exiled with Eye of the Storm. For each copy, the player may cast the copy without paying its mana cost.', 'Whenever a player draws a card, that player loses 2 life unless they pay {2}.', 'Whenever a source an opponent controls deals damage to you, that player sacrifices a permanent.', 'Whenever an Equipment enters the battlefield under your control, you may draw a card.\\nMetalcraft — Equipment you control have equip {0} as long as you control three or more artifacts.', "Whenever an ability of equipped creature is activated, if it isn't a mana ability, copy that ability. You may choose new targets for the copy.\\nEquip {3}", 'Whenever an opponent casts a spell, that player draws seven cards.', 'Whenever an opponent discards a card, you may draw a card.', "Whenever an opponent discards a card, you may put a quest counter on Quest for the Nihil Stone.\\nAt the beginning of each opponent's upkeep, if that player has no cards in hand and Quest for the Nihil Stone has two or more quest counters on it, you may have that player lose 5 life.", 'Whenever an opponent draws a card, if you control a red permanent, you may have Kederekt Parasite deal 1 damage to that player.', 'Whenever an opponent loses life, you gain that much life.', 'Whenever another Goblin you control becomes blocked, sacrifice it. If you do, it deals 4 damage to each creature blocking it.\\nSacrifice two Mountains: Create two 1/1 red Goblin creature tokens.', 'Whenever another Human enters the battlefield under your control, put a +1/+1 counter on Champion of the Parish.', 'Whenever another creature enters the battlefield under your control, put a +1/+1 counter on that creature and a +1/+1 counter on Juniper Order Ranger.', 'Whenever another creature you control dies, create a Treasure token. (It\'s an artifact with "{T}, Sacrifice this artifact: Add one mana of any color.")', 'Whenever another nontoken creature enters the battlefield under your control, investigate.\\n{T}, Sacrifice X Clues: Target opponent reveals the top X cards of their library. You may put a nonland permanent card with mana value X or less from among them onto the battlefield under your control. That player puts the rest on the bottom of their library in a random order.', "Whenever equipped creature deals combat damage, put two charge counters on Umezawa's Jitte.\\nRemove a charge counter from Umezawa's Jitte: Choose one —\\n• Equipped creature gets +2/+2 until end of turn.\\n• Target creature gets -1/-1 until end of turn.\\n• You gain 2 life.\\nEquip {2}", 'Whenever you cast a Druid spell, you may draw a card.\\nTap seven untapped Druids you control: Gain control of all lands target player controls.', "Whenever you cast a creature spell that has an Adventure, draw a card. (It doesn't need to have gone on the adventure first.)", "Whenever you cast a creature spell, create X 1/1 black Thrull creature tokens, where X is that spell's mana value.\\nWhen you control seven or more Thrulls, sacrifice Endrek Sahr, Master Breeder.", 'Whenever you cast a creature spell, create a 3/3 green Beast creature token.\\nWhenever you cast a noncreature spell, put three +1/+1 counters on target creature you control.\\nLandfall — Whenever a land enters the battlefield under your control, you gain 3 life.', 'Whenever you cast a creature spell, you may put a quest counter on Quest for the Holy Relic.\\nRemove five quest counters from Quest for the Holy Relic and sacrifice it: Search your library for an Equipment card, put it onto the battlefield, attach it to a creature you control, then shuffle.', "Whenever you cast a historic spell, you may pay {1}. If you do, create a token that's a copy of Mishra's Self-Replicator. (Artifacts, legendaries, and Sagas are historic.)", 'Whenever you cast a noncreature spell, put a +1/+1 counter on Deeproot Champion.', 'Whenever you cast a noncreature spell, put a lore counter on Scroll of the Masters.\\n{3}, {T}: Target creature you control gets +1/+1 until end of turn for each lore counter on Scroll of the Masters.', "Whenever you cast a noncreature spell, surveil 1. (Look at the top card of your library. You may put that card into your graveyard.)\\nDelirium — As long as there are four or more card types among cards in your graveyard, Dragon's Rage Channeler gets +2/+2, has flying, and attacks each combat if able.", "Whenever you cast a permanent spell with a mana cost that contains {X}, double the value of X.\\nWhenever you cast an instant or sorcery spell or activate an ability, if that spell's mana cost or that ability's activation cost contains {X}, copy that spell or ability. You may choose new targets for the copy.", 'Whenever you cast a planeswalker spell, you gain 1 life.\\n{T}: Add {C}.\\n{1}, {T}: Add two mana of different colors. Spend this mana only to cast planeswalker spells.', 'Whenever you cast a spell, put the cards in your hand on the bottom of your library in any order, then draw that many cards.', 'Whenever you cast a spell, you may put two +1/+1 counters on Witch-Maw Nephilim.\\nWhenever Witch-Maw Nephilim attacks, it gains trample until end of turn if its power is 10 or greater.', 'Whenever you cast an Adventure instant or sorcery spell, copy it. You may choose new targets for the copy.', 'Whenever you cast an artifact spell, you may search your graveyard, hand, and/or library for a card with the same name as that spell and put it onto the battlefield. If you search your library this way, shuffle.', 'Whenever you cast an enchantment spell, you get an experience counter.\\n{1}{W}{B}: Create a white and black Spirit enchantment creature token. It has "This creature\'s power and toughness are each equal to the number of experience counters you have."', 'Whenever you cast an instant or sorcery spell that has the same name as a card in your graveyard, you may put a quest counter on Pyromancer Ascension.\\nWhenever you cast an instant or sorcery spell while Pyromancer Ascension has two or more quest counters on it, you may copy that spell. You may choose new targets for the copy.', 'Whenever you cast an instant or sorcery spell with mana value greater than the number of experience counters you have, you get an experience counter.\\nInstant and sorcery spells you cast cost {1} less to cast for each experience counter you have.', 'Whenever you cast an instant or sorcery spell, Guttersnipe deals 2 damage to each opponent.', 'Whenever you cast an instant or sorcery spell, create a 1/1 red Elemental creature token.', 'Whenever you cast your first instant spell each turn, if Kalamax, the Stormsire is tapped, copy that spell. You may choose new targets for the copy.\\nWhenever you copy an instant spell, put a +1/+1 counter on Kalamax.', 'Whenever you discard a creature card, create a 2/2 black Zombie creature token.\\nWhenever you discard a land card, add {B}{B}.\\nWhenever you discard a noncreature, nonland card, draw a card.', 'Whenever you draw a card, put a foreshadow counter on Ominous Seas.\\nRemove eight foreshadow counters from Ominous Seas: Create an 8/8 blue Kraken creature token.\\nCycling {2} ({2}, Discard this card: Draw a card.)', 'Whenever you gain life, put a +1/+1 counter on Twinblade Paladin.\\nAs long as you have 25 or more life, Twinblade Paladin has double strike. (It deals both first-strike and regular combat damage.)', 'Whenever you tap a land for mana, add one mana of any type that land produced. (The types of mana are white, blue, black, red, green, and colorless.)\\nWhenever you cast a creature spell, draw a card.', 'While voting, you get an additional vote. (The votes can be for different choices or for the same choice.)', 'White spells you cast cost {1} less to cast.\\nBlue spells you cast cost {1} less to cast.\\nSpells your opponents cast cost {1} more to cast.', "Will of the council — Starting with you, each player votes for a nonland permanent you don't control. Exile each permanent with the most votes or tied for most votes.", 'Will of the council — Starting with you, each player votes for time or knowledge. If time gets more votes, take an extra turn after this one. If knowledge gets more votes or the vote is tied, draw three cards.', "Wither (This deals damage to creatures in the form of -1/-1 counters.)\\nWhenever Stigma Lasher deals damage to a player, that player can't gain life for the rest of the game.", 'Workhorse enters the battlefield with four +1/+1 counters on it.\\nRemove a +1/+1 counter from Workhorse: Add {C}.', 'Worn Powerstone enters the battlefield tapped.\\n{T}: Add {C}{C}.', "X can't be 0.\\nTarget spell's controller exiles it with X delay counters on it.\\nAt the beginning of each of that player's upkeeps, if that card is exiled, remove a delay counter from it. If the card has no delay counters on it, the player puts it onto the stack as a copy of the original spell.", "Xantcha, Sleeper Agent enters the battlefield under the control of an opponent of your choice.\\nXantcha attacks each combat if able and can't attack its owner or planeswalkers its owner controls.\\n{3}: Xantcha's controller loses 2 life and you draw a card. Any player may activate this ability.", "You and target spell's controller bid life. You start the bidding with a bid of 1. In turn order, each player may top the high bid. The bidding ends if the high bid stands. The high bidder loses life equal to the high bid. If you win the bidding, counter that spell.", "You can't cast more than one spell each turn.\\nYou may play lands and cast spells from your graveyard.\\nIf a card would be put into your graveyard from anywhere, exile it instead.", 'You draw three cards and you lose 3 life.', 'You gain 1 life for each player.\\nHaunt (When this spell card is put into a graveyard after resolving, exile it haunting target creature.)\\nWhen the creature Benediction of Moons haunts dies, you gain 1 life for each player.', 'You gain 2 life. Then if you have more life than an opponent, draw a card.\\nRebound (If you cast this spell from your hand, exile it as it resolves. At the beginning of your next upkeep, you may cast this card from exile without paying its mana cost.)', 'You gain 3 life for each creature attacking you.', "You gain twice X life. Put Sanguine Sacrament on the bottom of its owner's library.", 'You have no maximum hand size.', 'You have no maximum hand size.\\n{T}: Add {C}.', 'You may activate abilities of creatures you control as though those creatures had haste.\\n{1}, {T}: Untap target creature.', 'You may cast Ghitu Fire as though it had flash if you pay {2} more to cast it. (You may cast it any time you could cast an instant.)\\nGhitu Fire deals X damage to any target.', 'You may cast Necromancy as though it had flash. If you cast it any time a sorcery couldn\'t have been cast, the controller of the permanent it becomes sacrifices it at the beginning of the next cleanup step.\\nWhen Necromancy enters the battlefield, if it\'s on the battlefield, it becomes an Aura with "enchant creature put onto the battlefield with Necromancy." Put target creature card from a graveyard onto the battlefield under your control and attach Necromancy to it. When Necromancy leaves the battlefield, that creature\'s controller sacrifices it.', "You may cast Rout as though it had flash if you pay {2} more to cast it. (You may cast it any time you could cast an instant.)\\nDestroy all creatures. They can't be regenerated.", 'You may cast spells as though they had flash.', "You may choose not to untap Amber Prison during your untap step.\\n{4}, {T}: Tap target artifact, creature, or land. That permanent doesn't untap during its controller's untap step for as long as Amber Prison remains tapped.", 'You may choose not to untap Endoskeleton during your untap step.\\n{2}, {T}: Target creature gets +0/+3 for as long as Endoskeleton remains tapped.', "You may exile a black card from your hand rather than pay this spell's mana cost.\\nTarget player reveals their hand. You choose a nonland card from it. That player discards that card.", "You may exile a red card with mana value X from your hand rather than pay this spell's mana cost.\\nTarget creature gets +X/+0 until end of turn.", "You may have Deathcoil Wurm assign its combat damage as though it weren't blocked.", 'You may have Jwari Shapeshifter enter the battlefield as a copy of any Ally creature on the battlefield.', 'You may have Vesuva enter the battlefield tapped as a copy of any land on the battlefield.', "You may pay 6 life and sacrifice three black creatures rather than pay this spell's mana cost.\\nFlying, trample", 'You may pay {0} rather than pay the mana cost for Zombie creature spells you cast.', 'You may pay {W}{U}{B}{R}{G} rather than pay the mana cost for spells that you cast.', "You may play an additional land on each of your turns.\\n{R}{G}, Return a land you control to its owner's hand: Target creature gains trample until end of turn.", 'You may tap or untap target permanent, then you may tap or untap another target permanent.', 'You win the game if you control a land of each basic land type and a creature of each color.', "Your opponents can't cast spells this turn.", 'Your opponents can\'t gain life.\\n[−2]: Create a 1/1 red Devil creature token with "When this creature dies, it deals 1 damage to any target."', "Zendikar Incarnate's power is equal to the number of lands you control.", 'Zombies you control get +1/+0.\\nAt the beginning of your end step, if a creature died this turn, you may pay {1}{B}. If you do, create a 2/2 black Zombie creature token.', "[+1]: Chandra Nalaar deals 1 damage to target player or planeswalker.\\n[−X]: Chandra Nalaar deals X damage to target creature.\\n[−8]: Chandra Nalaar deals 10 damage to target player or planeswalker and each creature that player or that planeswalker's controller controls.", '[+1]: Create a 1/1 colorless Thopter artifact creature token with flying.\\n[0]: Draw a card. If you control three or more artifacts, draw two cards instead.\\n[−9]: You get an emblem with "At the beginning of your end step, search your library for a permanent card, put it onto the battlefield, then shuffle."', '[+1]: Draw a card. At the beginning of the next end step, untap up to two lands.\\n[−3]: Put target nonland permanent into its owner\'s library third from the top.\\n[−8]: You get an emblem with "Whenever you draw a card, exile target permanent an opponent controls."', '[+1]: Exile the top three cards of your library. Creature cards exiled this way gain "You may cast this card from exile as long as you control a Lukka planeswalker."\\n[−2]: Exile target creature you control, then reveal cards from the top of your library until you reveal a creature card with higher mana value. Put that card onto the battlefield and the rest on the bottom of your library in a random order.\\n[−7]: Each creature you control deals damage equal to its power to each opponent.', '[+1]: Exile up to two target cards from a single graveyard. You gain 2 life if at least one creature card was exiled this way.\\n[−1]: Exile target nonland permanent with mana value 1 or less.\\n[−5]: Kaya, Orzhov Usurper deals damage to target player equal to the number of cards that player owns in exile and you gain that much life.', '[+1]: Look at the top four cards of your library. You may reveal a creature or land card from among them and put it into your hand. Put the rest on the bottom of your library in a random order.\\n[−3]: Destroy target artifact, enchantment, or creature with flying.\\n[−8]: You get an emblem with "Creatures you control get +2/+2 and have vigilance, trample, and indestructible."', '[+1]: Return up to one target land card from your graveyard to your hand.\\n[−1]: Wrenn and Six deals 1 damage to any target.\\n[−7]: You get an emblem with "Instant and sorcery cards in your graveyard have retrace." (You may cast instant and sorcery cards from your graveyard by discarding a land card in addition to paying their other costs.)', "[+1]: Scry 1. Saheeli Rai deals 1 damage to each opponent.\\n[−2]: Create a token that's a copy of target artifact or creature you control, except it's an artifact in addition to its other types. That token gains haste. Exile it at the beginning of the next end step.\\n[−7]: Search your library for up to three artifact cards with different names, put them onto the battlefield, then shuffle.", "[+1]: Search your library for a card named Nissa's Chosen, put it onto the battlefield, then shuffle.\\n[+1]: You gain 2 life for each Elf you control.\\n[−7]: Search your library for any number of Elf creature cards, put them onto the battlefield, then shuffle.", '[+1]: Until end of turn, Gideon, Ally of Zendikar becomes a 5/5 Human Soldier Ally creature with indestructible that\'s still a planeswalker. Prevent all damage that would be dealt to him this turn.\\n[0]: Create a 2/2 white Knight Ally creature token.\\n[−4]: You get an emblem with "Creatures you control get +1/+1."', '[+1]: Up to one target creature gets -2/-1 until your next turn.\\n[−2]: Mill two cards, then you may return a creature card from your graveyard to your hand.\\n[−7]: You get an emblem with "At the beginning of your end step, create X 2/2 black Zombie creature tokens, where X is two plus the number of Zombies you control."', '[+1]: You gain life equal to the number of creatures you control plus the number of planeswalkers you control.\\n[−2]: Create a 2/2 white Cat Soldier creature token named Ajani\'s Pridemate with "Whenever you gain life, put a +1/+1 counter on Ajani\'s Pridemate."\\n[0]: If you have at least 15 life more than your starting life total, exile Ajani, Strength of the Pride and each artifact and creature your opponents control.', '[+2]: Create a 1/1 green Elf Druid creature token with "{T}: Add {G}."\\n[−2]: Destroy target artifact or enchantment.\\n[−6]: Draw a card for each green creature you control.\\nFreyalise, Llanowar\'s Fury can be your commander.', '[+2]: Create a 1/1 white Kor Soldier creature token. You may attach an Equipment you control to it.\\n[−2]: You may put an Equipment card from your hand or graveyard onto the battlefield.\\n[−10]: Create a colorless Equipment artifact token named Stoneforged Blade. It has indestructible, "Equipped creature gets +5/+5 and has double strike," and equip {0}.\\nNahiri, the Lithomancer can be your commander.', '[+2]: Create two 0/1 black Thrull creature tokens.\\n[+1]: You may sacrifice another creature or planeswalker. If you do, draw two cards, then draw another card if the sacrificed permanent was a commander.\\n[−10]: Gain control of all commanders. Put all commanders from the command zone onto the battlefield under your control.\\nTevesh Szat, Doom of Fools can be your commander.\\nPartner', '[+2]: During target player\'s next turn, each creature that player controls attacks if able.\\n[−2]: Rowan Kenrith deals 3 damage to each tapped creature target player controls.\\n[−8]: Target player gets an emblem with "Whenever you activate an ability that isn\'t a mana ability, copy it. You may choose new targets for the copy."\\nPartner with Will Kenrith\\nRowan Kenrith can be your commander.', '[+2]: Put a +1/+1 counter on each of up to two target creatures.\\n[−2]: Search your library and/or graveyard for a card named Sunlit Hoplite and put it onto the battlefield. If you search your library this way, shuffle.\\n[−8]: Until end of turn, creatures you control gain flying and get +X/+X, where X is your devotion to white.', "[+2]: Sorin Markov deals 2 damage to any target and you gain 2 life.\\n[−3]: Target opponent's life total becomes 10.\\n[−7]: You control target player during that player's next turn.", '[+2]: Until your next turn, up to two target creatures each have base power and toughness 0/3 and lose all abilities.\\n[−2]: Target player draws two cards. Until your next turn, instant, sorcery, and planeswalker spells that player casts cost {2} less to cast.\\n[−8]: Target player gets an emblem with "Whenever you cast an instant or sorcery spell, copy it. You may choose new targets for the copy."\\nPartner with Rowan Kenrith\\nWill Kenrith can be your commander.', '[+4]: Target player exiles a card from their hand.\\n[−3]: Exile target permanent.\\n[−14]: Restart the game, leaving in exile all non-Aura permanent cards exiled with Karn Liberated. Then put those cards onto the battlefield under your control.', "[0]: Exile Kaya, Ghost Assassin or up to one target creature. Return that card to the battlefield under its owner's control at the beginning of your next upkeep. You lose 2 life.\\n[−1]: Each opponent loses 2 life and you gain 2 life.\\n[−2]: Each opponent discards a card and you draw a card.", '[0]: Exile Kaya, Ghost Haunter haunting target creature for as long as that creature remains on the battlefield.\\n[−1]: You get an emblem with, "At the beginning of your upkeep, this emblem deals 3 damage to the owner of target haunted creature."\\n[−2]: You get an emblem with, "At the beginning of your upkeep, gain control of target haunted creature for as long as it remains haunted."', "{0}: Until end of turn, Jodah's Avenger gets -1/-1 and gains your choice of double strike, protection from red, vigilance, or shadow. (A creature with shadow can block or be blocked by only creatures with shadow.)", '{1}, Sacrifice a Scarecrow: Draw a card.\\n{4}, {T}: Return target artifact creature card from your graveyard to the battlefield.', '{1}, Sacrifice a nontoken artifact: Create a 1/1 blue Thopter artifact creature token with flying. You gain 1 life.', "{1}, {T}, Discard a card: Put a study counter on Grimoire of the Dead.\\n{T}, Remove three study counters from Grimoire of the Dead and sacrifice it: Put all creature cards from all graveyards onto the battlefield under your control. They're black Zombies in addition to their other colors and types.", '{1}, {T}, Discard a card: Target noncreature artifact becomes an artifact creature with power and toughness each equal to its mana value until end of turn. (It retains its abilities.)', "{1}, {T}: Acorn Catapult deals 1 damage to any target. That permanent's controller or that player creates a 1/1 green Squirrel creature token.", '{1}, {T}: Exile any number of cards from your hand face down. Put that many cards from the top of your library into your hand. Then look at the exiled cards and put them on top of your library in any order.', "{1}, {T}: Exile target creature you control.\\n{7}, {T}: Exile target creature you don't control.\\nWhen Helvault is put into a graveyard from the battlefield, return all cards exiled with it to the battlefield under their owners' control.", "{1}, {T}: Return target creature to its owner's hand unless its controller pays {1}.", "{1}, {T}: Roll a d4 and create a number of Treasure tokens equal to the result. The player to your right gains control of Bucknard's Everfull Purse.", "{1}: Look at the top three cards of your library, then put them back in any order.\\n{T}: Draw a card, then put Sensei's Divining Top on top of its owner's library.", "{1}: Return target land you control to its owner's hand.\\n{1}, Discard a land card: Draw a card.", '{1}: The next time you would draw a card this turn, Words of War deals 2 damage to any target instead.', '{1}: Untap Staff of Domination.\\n{2}, {T}: You gain 1 life.\\n{3}, {T}: Untap target creature.\\n{4}, {T}: Tap target creature.\\n{5}, {T}: Draw a card.', '{1}{B}, {T}, Discard a card: Choose a card name. Exile the top six cards of your library, then reveal cards from the top of your library until you reveal a card with the chosen name. Put that card into your hand and exile all other cards revealed this way.', "{1}{B}: Exile target card from an opponent's graveyard. If no cards are in that graveyard, flip Nezumi Graverobber.", '{1}{G}: Dire Wolf Prowler gets +2/+2 and gains haste until end of turn. Activate only once each turn.', '{1}{G}: Target Kavu creature gets -1/+1 until end of turn.', '{1}{R}, Sacrifice a creature: Blood Rites deals 2 damage to any target.', '{1}{R}, Sacrifice a creature: Destroy target nonbasic land.', "{1}{R}, {T}: Destroy target artifact. Viashino Heretic deals damage to that artifact's controller equal to the artifact's mana value.", "{1}{U}{R}: Return Etherium-Horn Sorcerer to its owner's hand.\\nCascade (When you cast this spell, exile cards from the top of your library until you exile a nonland card that costs less. You may cast it without paying its mana cost. Put the exiled cards on the bottom of your library in a random order.)", '{1}{W}: Search your library for an enchantment card and reveal that card. Put it into your hand, then discard a card at random. Then shuffle.\\n{1}{U}: Search your library for an instant card and reveal that card. Put it into your hand, then discard a card at random. Then shuffle.', "{2}, Exile a nonland card from your hand: Put four time counters on the exiled card. If it doesn't have suspend, it gains suspend. (At the beginning of your upkeep, remove a time counter from that card. When the last is removed, cast it without paying its mana cost. If it's a creature, it has haste.)", '{2}, {T}, Choose flying, first strike, trample, or shadow: Until end of turn, target creature with the chosen ability loses it and another target creature gains it.', '{2}, {T}, Sacrifice Expedition Map: Search your library for a land card, reveal it, put it into your hand, then shuffle.', "{2}, {T}, Sacrifice Wayfarer's Bauble: Search your library for a basic land card, put that card onto the battlefield tapped, then shuffle.", '{2}, {T}, Sacrifice a creature: Draw a card.', '{2}, {T}: Create a 0/1 colorless Pest artifact creature token.', '{2}, {T}: Draw a card. Activate only if you have no cards in hand.', "{2}, {T}: Draw a card. Activate only if you've cast a noncreature spell this turn.", '{2}, {T}: Search your library for a card named Festering Newt or Bubbling Cauldron, put it onto the battlefield tapped, then shuffle.', '{2}: Until end of turn, target nonartifact creature gets +1/+0 and becomes an artifact in addition to its other types.', '{2}{G}, {T}, Put a verse counter on Yisan, the Wanderer Bard: Search your library for a creature card with mana value equal to the number of verse counters on Yisan, put it onto the battlefield, then shuffle.', "{2}{R}, {T}: Create a token that's a copy of target creature card in your graveyard, except it's an artifact in addition to its other types. It gains haste. Sacrifice it at the beginning of the next end step.", '{2}{U}{U}, {T}: Draw a card for each Wizard you control.', '{2}{U}{U}: Draw a card.', '{2}{U}{U}: Exchange control of Phyrexian Infiltrator and target creature. (This effect lasts indefinitely.)', '{2}{W}, {T}, Sacrifice Nova Cleric: Destroy all enchantments.', "{2}{W}{U}: Exile target creature. Return that card to the battlefield under its owner's control at the beginning of the next end step.", "{3}, {T}, Sacrifice a creature: Reveal a number of cards from the top of your library equal to the sacrificed creature's power. Put one into your hand and exile the rest.", '{3}, {T}: Double the amount of each type of unspent mana you have.', '{3}, {T}: Investigate. (Create a Clue token. It\'s an artifact with "{2}, Sacrifice this artifact: Draw a card.")', '{3}, {T}: Search your library for a Goblin permanent card, put it onto the battlefield, then shuffle.', '{3}, {T}: Search your library for a Merfolk permanent card, put it onto the battlefield, then shuffle.', '{3}, {T}: Tap target creature. Gain control of that creature instead if you control artifacts named Scepter of Empires and Throne of Empires.', '{3}: Exile target creature you control.\\nSacrifice Cold Storage: Return each creature card exiled with Cold Storage to the battlefield under your control.', "{3}{R}: Target opponent reveals a card at random from their hand. Planeswalker's Fury deals damage equal to that card's mana value to that player. Activate only as a sorcery.", '{3}{U}{U}: Turn Mischievous Quanar face down.\\nMorph {1}{U}{U} (You may cast this card face down as a 2/2 creature for {3}. Turn it face up any time for its morph cost.)\\nWhen Mischievous Quanar is turned face up, copy target instant or sorcery spell. You may choose new targets for that copy.', '{4}, {T}, Sacrifice a creature: Fodder Cannon deals 4 damage to target creature.', '{4}, {T}: Create a 2/2 colorless Shapeshifter creature token with changeling. (It has every creature type.)', '{4}, {T}: Put a divinity counter on target permanent other than That Which Was Taken.\\nEach permanent with a divinity counter on it has indestructible.', '{4}{B}: Put target creature card from a graveyard onto the battlefield under your control.', "{4}{G}{W}: Create a 3/3 green Centaur creature token.\\n{2}{G}{W}: Populate. (Create a token that's a copy of a creature token you control.)", '{6}, {T}: Search your library for a card, put that card into your hand, then shuffle.', '{B}, Discard a creature card: Return target creature card from your graveyard to your hand.', '{B}, Sacrifice Urborg Panther: Destroy target creature blocking Urborg Panther.\\nSacrifice a creature named Feral Shadow, a creature named Breathstealer, and Urborg Panther: Search your library for a card named Spirit of the Night, put that card onto the battlefield, then shuffle.', "{B}: Endling gains menace until end of turn.\\n{B}: Endling gains deathtouch until end of turn.\\n{B}: Endling gains undying until end of turn. (When this creature dies, if it had no +1/+1 counters on it, return it to the battlefield under its owner's control with a +1/+1 counter on it.)\\n{1}: Endling gets +1/-1 or -1/+1 until end of turn.", '{B}: Regenerate Phyrexian Monitor.', '{B}{B}{B}, {T}: Destroy target land. If that land was nonbasic, untap Helldozer.', '{G}, {T}: Reveal cards from the top of your library until you reveal a basic land card. Put that card into your hand and all other cards revealed this way into your graveyard.', '{G}: Regenerate another target Elf.\\n{2}{G}{G}{G}: Elf creatures you control get +3/+3 and gain trample until end of turn.', "{G}{G}, Sacrifice Rootrunner: Put target land on top of its owner's library.\\nSoulshift 3 (When this creature dies, you may return target Spirit card with mana value 3 or less from your graveyard to your hand.)", "{G}{U}: Target creature can't be blocked this turn. If that creature is a Snake, it gets +2/+2 until end of turn.", "{R}, {T}, Discard a card: Destroy target blue permanent.\\n{1}{R}, {T}, Discard a card: Jaya Ballard, Task Mage deals 3 damage to any target. A creature dealt damage this way can't be regenerated this turn.\\n{5}{R}{R}, {T}, Discard a card: Jaya Ballard deals 6 damage to each creature and each player.", '{R}: You may put a creature card from your hand onto the battlefield. That creature gains haste. Sacrifice the creature at the beginning of the next end step.', '{T}, Remove a component counter from Component Pouch: Add two mana of different colors.\\n{T}: Roll a d20.\\n1—9 | Put a component counter on Component Pouch.\\n10—20 | Put two component counters on Component Pouch.', '{T}, Sacrifice Mimic: Add one mana of any color.\\n{2}: Mimic becomes a Shapeshifter artifact creature with base power and toughness 3/3 until end of turn.', "{T}, Sacrifice Nihil Spellbomb: Exile target player's graveyard.\\nWhen Nihil Spellbomb is put into a graveyard from the battlefield, you may pay {B}. If you do, draw a card.", '{T}, Sacrifice a Forest: Add three mana in any combination of {R} and/or {G}.', '{T}, Sacrifice a creature: Create a Food token. If the sacrificed creature\'s toughness was 4 or greater, create two Food tokens instead. (They\'re artifacts with "{2}, {T}, Sacrifice this artifact: You gain 3 life.")', '{T}, Sacrifice a land: Destroy target land.', '{T}, Tap X untapped artifacts you control: Look at the top X cards of your library. Put one of those cards into your hand and the rest into your graveyard.\\nPartner (You can have two commanders if both have partner.)', '{T}: Add one mana of any color that a land an opponent controls could produce.', '{T}: Add one mana of any color.\\n{T}: Put a charge counter on Coalition Relic.\\nAt the beginning of your precombat main phase, remove all charge counters from Coalition Relic. Add one mana of any color for each charge counter removed this way.', '{T}: Add {C} for each artifact you control named Powerstone Shard.', '{T}: Add {C}.', "{T}: Add {C}.\\n{1}: Mishra's Factory becomes a 2/2 Assembly-Worker artifact creature until end of turn. It's still a land.\\n{T}: Target Assembly-Worker creature gets +1/+1 until end of turn.", '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{1}{R}, {T}: Create a 0/1 red Kobold creature token named Kobolds of Kher Keep.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{1}{S}, {T}: Look at the top card of your library. If that card is snow, you may reveal it and put it into your hand. ({S} can be paid with one mana from a snow source.)', "{T}: Add {C}.\\n{1}{U}, {T}: Return target Wizard you control to its owner's hand.", '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{2}, {T}: Choose a color. Add an amount of mana of that color equal to your devotion to that color. (Your devotion to a color is the number of mana symbols of that color in the mana costs of permanents you control.)', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{2}{R}, {T}: Shivan Gorge deals 1 damage to each opponent.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{3}{W}{B}, {T}: Target player loses 1 life and you gain 1 life.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{4}{S}, {T}, Sacrifice Mouth of Ronom: It deals 4 damage to target creature. ({S} can be paid with one mana from a snow source.)', "{T}: Add {C}.\\n{5}, {T}, Exile Underdark Rift: Roll a d10. Put target artifact, creature, or planeswalker into its owner's library just beneath the top X cards of that library, where X is the result. Activate only as a sorcery.", '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{7}, {T}: Create a 2/2 colorless Assembly-Worker artifact creature token.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{B}, {T}: Put target Zombie card from your graveyard on top of your library.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{T}, Pay 1 life: Add {G}.\\n{1}{G}{G}, {T}, Sacrifice a Desert: Target creature gets +3/+3 until end of turn. Activate only as a sorcery.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{T}, Sacrifice Command Beacon: Put your commander into your hand from the command zone.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{T}, Sacrifice Petrified Field: Return target land card from your graveyard to your hand.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{T}, Sacrifice a creature: Add {B}{B}.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{T}, Sacrifice a creature: You gain 1 life.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{T}: Add {C}{C}. Spend this mana only to cast colorless Eldrazi spells or activate abilities of colorless Eldrazi.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{T}: Desert deals 1 damage to target attacking creature. Activate only during the end of combat step.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{T}: Roll the planar die. Activate only as a sorcery.', '{T}: Add {C}{C}. Ancient Tomb deals 2 damage to you.', '{T}: Add {G} for each Elf on the battlefield.', '{T}: Add {G} or {W}.\\n{G}{W}: Selesnya Keyrune becomes a 3/3 green and white Wolf artifact creature until end of turn.', '{T}: Add {G}.', '{T}: Add {G}.\\nPut a -1/-1 counter on Devoted Druid: Untap Devoted Druid.', '{T}: Add {G}.\\n{G}, {T}: Target legendary creature gets +1/+1 until end of turn.', '{T}: Add {R}.', '{T}: Add {R}. Barbarian Ring deals 1 damage to you.\\nThreshold — {R}, {T}, Sacrifice Barbarian Ring: It deals 2 damage to any target. Activate only if seven or more cards are in your graveyard.', '{T}: Add {R}.\\n{R}, {T}: Target legendary creature gains first strike until end of turn.', '{T}: Add {U}.\\n{2}{U}: Put an hour counter on Midnight Clock.\\nAt the beginning of each upkeep, put an hour counter on Midnight Clock.\\nWhen the twelfth hour counter is put on Midnight Clock, shuffle your hand and graveyard into your library, then draw seven cards. Exile Midnight Clock.', '{T}: Add {W}.', '{T}: Add {W}.\\n{W}, {T}: Prevent the next 2 damage that would be dealt to target legendary creature this turn.', '{T}: Another target creature you control gains protection from colorless or from the color of your choice until end of turn.', "{T}: Destroy target artifact or creature. That permanent's controller gains control of Starke of Rath. (This effect lasts indefinitely.)", '{T}: Draw a card, then discard a card.\\n{2}{U}{B}, {T}, Sacrifice Obsessive Stitcher: Return target creature card from your graveyard to the battlefield.', "{T}: Exile the bottom card of target player's graveyard.\\n{1}, Sacrifice Phyrexian Furnace: Exile target card from a graveyard. Draw a card.", "{T}: Heartless Hidetsugu deals damage to each player equal to half that player's life total, rounded down.", '{T}: Mill two cards.\\n{2}, Exile Perpetual Timepiece: Shuffle any number of target cards from your graveyard into your library.', '{T}: Put target creature card from your graveyard on top of your library. Activate only during your turn, before attackers are declared.', '{T}: Target creature other than Serendib Sorcerer has base power and toughness 0/2 until end of turn.', "{T}: Target creature you control with toughness less than Stone Giant's power gains flying until end of turn. Destroy that creature at the beginning of the next end step.", '{T}: Target legendary creature gets +2/+2 until end of turn.', '{T}: Untap two target lands.', '{U}, {T}, Sacrifice a creature or enchantment: Counter target spell.', "{U}, {T}: Draw two cards.\\n{R}, {T}, Discard a card: Mercurial Chemister deals damage to target creature equal to the discarded card's mana value.", '{U}{B}, {T}: Create a 1/1 blue and black Zombie Wizard creature token.\\n{U}{U}{B}{B}: Target player loses X life and mills X cards, where X is the number of Zombies you control.', '{U}{U}, {T}: Gain control of target legendary permanent. (This effect lasts indefinitely.)', "{U}{U}, {T}: Target creature phases out. (While it's phased out, it's treated as though it doesn't exist. It phases in before its controller untaps during their next untap step.)", "{W}, {T}: Calming Licid loses this ability and becomes an Aura enchantment with enchant creature. Attach it to target creature. You may pay {W} to end this effect.\\nEnchanted creature can't attack.", '{W}, {T}: Exile target Skeleton, Vampire, or Zombie.', "{W}{U}{B}{R}{G}: Exile target permanent.\\nIf Legacy Weapon would be put into a graveyard from anywhere, reveal Legacy Weapon and shuffle it into its owner's library instead.", '{X}, {T}: Tap X target lands.', '{X}: Crypt Rats deals X damage to each creature and each player. Spend only black mana on X.', '{X}{R}, {T}, Discard a card: Destroy all artifacts with mana value X or less.', "{X}{X}{G}: Monstrosity X. (If this creature isn't monstrous, put X +1/+1 counters on it and it becomes monstrous.)\\nWhen Polukranos, World Eater becomes monstrous, it deals X damage divided as you choose among any number of target creatures your opponents control. Each of those creatures deals damage equal to its power to Polukranos."]
flavor: ['". . . and furthermore . . ."', '"A display of humility is required of those who still possess such frailties."\\n—Elesh Norn, Grand Cenobite', '"A gargoyle\'s meat can be carved with an ordinary cleaver, but for its petrous hide . . ."\\n—Asmoranomardicadaistinaculdacar, *The Underworld Cookbook*', '"A rare and fascinating phenomenon."\\n—Tamiyo', '"A regression to ancient forms? A glimpse of future evolutions? Or a fleeting alteration of the present?"\\n—Vorel of the Hull Clade', '"Above the waves you may be mighty indeed, but down here you belong to me."', '"Abzan, Jeskai, Sultai, Mardu, Temur—names lost to history, yet worthy of further study."\\n—Narset', '"Accursed scarecrow! Sending folk in every direction is the same as sending them nowhere at all."\\n—Corliss the Wanderer', '"After four thousand years, you learn to plan for betrayal."\\n—Urza', '"After the people flee, but before the enemy arrives—that\'s grabbin\' time."', '"All are welcome in the angels\' light."', '"All memory of your existence will be wiped from reality. You will die, and no one will mourn."\\n—Memnarch', '"All my spells smell like burnt hair lately."\\n—Jaya Ballard, task mage', '"All that concerns me is the vampires\' sense of smell and those freezing Nephalian nights."', '"As flies to wanton boys, are we to the gods. They kill us for their sport."\\n—William Shakespeare, *King Lear*', '"As the sun sets to make way for dawn, so we turn to darkness to bring about the coming salvation."', '"Avacyn has abandoned us! We have nothing left except what we can take!"', '"Barrin taught me that the hardest lessons to grasp are the ones you\'ve already learned."\\n—Ertai, wizard adept', '"Beauty to the eye does not always translate to the touch."\\n—Naimah, Femeref philosopher', '"Before the war, we prayed to Kataki to sharpen our swords and harden our armor. Without his blessing our weapons are all but useless against the kami hordes."\\n—Kenzo the Hardhearted', '"Behold blessed perfection."\\n—Sheoldred, Whispering One', '"Beings of the rifts are not natural. No longer will these abominations tread upon the body of Gaea."', '"Better for a doun to lose its cenn than its springjacks."', '"By this glyph I affirm your role."\\n—Urza, to Karn', '"Cherish these last moments. Though your miserable life has come to nothing, I have given it a magnificent end."', '"Dead or alive, my creations are stronger than Jin-Gitaxias\'s septic minions."\\n—Vorinclex, Voice of Hunger', '"Death tried to uncrown me. But now I return, king of a greater realm."', '"Debt and death sound so similar, and thrulls are so hard of hearing. Mistakes are inevitable."\\n—Milana, Orzhov prelate', '"Did Purphoros bless Maikal because of his rage? Or did Maikal\'s rage blossom after he\'d been blessed? Only the gods know."\\n—Eocles, oracle of Purphoros', '"Die. But die knowing that your pathetic life will yield a great bounty for me."\\n—Zul Ashur, lich lord', '"Do not flinch from studying the horrors of the past. History\'s most important lessons are cloaked in terror and tragedy."\\n—Augusta, Lorehold dean', '"Do not underestimate the power of many against one."\\n—Sidar Jabari', '"Each tooth is the length of a horse, and new ones grow in every sixteen days. Let\'s get a closer look!"\\n—Vivien Reid', '"Each year that passes rings you inwardly with memory and might. Wield your heart, and the world will tremble."', '"End this. What I seek is far greater."\\n—Elesh Norn, Grand Cenobite', '"Etherium is limited. Innovation is not."\\n—Tezzeret', '"Even a dragon is humble as a kitten if it thinks itself a slave."', '"Every choice is a joy."', '"Everybody but me—CHARGE!"', '"Everyone should owe you something."\\n—Geth, Lord of the Vault', '"Everything the wise woman learned she wrote in a book, and when the pages were black with ink, she took white ink and began again."\\n—Karn, silver golem', '"Fear holds no place in faith\'s battle plan."', '"Fire cleanses as well as destroys; that is the nature of change."\\n—Oracle *en*-Vec', '"Focus an enemy\'s mind on what\'s already gone, and it\'s easier to take away more."\\n—Holux, stronghold racketeer', '"For all I have lost, for all who have fallen, I will render you to dust."\\n—Jared Carthalion', '"For the survival of our people, every conflict must now end in retreat."\\n—Pythor, Mirran resistance', '"For what are leaves but countless blades\\nTo fight a countless foe on high."\\n—Skyshroud hymn', '"Froggy fighter at the gate.\\nDraw your sword and meet your fate."\\n—Traditional children\'s rhyme', '"From void evolved Phyrexia. Great Yawgmoth, Father of Machines, saw its perfection. Thus the Grand Evolution began."\\n—*Phyrexian Scriptures*', '"Give me eight walkers, I\'ll give you the city."\\n—Dovin Baan', '"Gix doesn\'t want a people to rule but puppets to entertain his madness."\\n—Xantcha, Phyrexian outcast', '"Great peril demands formidable weaponry."\\n—Urza', '"He cocooned himself alone in his workshop for months. When he finally emerged, all broad grins and excited chatter, I knew he\'d found his answer."\\n—Barrin, master wizard', '"He is Yawgmoth\'s reward to me. I shall kill him a hundred times a day."\\n—Crovax, to Ertai', '"He steals power from treasure after treasure, and what does it do for the ouphe? Nothing."\\n—Jhoira', '"Headed to the wilds? Beware the dead riders who serve the Shadow Queen."\\n—Scalan, Edgewall innkeeper', '"Her people angered Zendikar, and they faced the land\'s wrath. That is why Nissa is the last of the animists."\\n—Numa, Joraga chieftain', '"Her voice is damnation, unyielding and certain."\\n—Phage the Untouchable', '"Her voice is disaster, painful and final."\\n—Matoc, lavamancer', '"Her voice is justice, clear and relentless."\\n—Akroma, angelic avenger', '"His energy is as boundless as the powerstones\'."\\n—Rebbec, architect of ascension', '"How have I angered nature that she would imprison me in a labyrinth of grass?"\\n—Kasib ibn Naji, Letters', '"Humanity has always envied the power of flight. So we took it."\\n—Scytha, aeromage', '"I appreciate the depravity of noble designs turned to devious ends."\\n—Tezzeret', '"I can think of *one* goblin it ain\'t so lucky for."\\n—Slobad, goblin tinkerer', '"I confer with Death itself. What could you possibly do to injure me?"\\n—Lord Dralnu', '"I craved enlightenment, and Crucius\'s etherium opened my eyes. I would share my sight with you, but first you must believe."', '"I do not fear death. I know my soul will rise to Starnheim, where I will feast forever among valkyries and heroes. Can you say the same?"', '"I do not miss sunlight. The very memory of it burns my eyes."\\n—Volrath', '"I do not teach. I simply reveal."\\n—Daudi, Femeref tutor', '"I don\'t like to speak ill of \'walkers . . . but just what did Teferi think he was doing?"\\n—Ertai, wizard adept', '"I done forgot more than you\'ll ever know, pipsqueak."\\n"Yeah—that\'s your problem."', '"I gazed once into that light. Now it burns in my mind, forever denying me rest."\\n—Riku of Two Reflections', '"I give them dreams so wondrous that they hesitate to return to the world of the conscious."\\n—Garild, merfolk mage', '"I have a plan. Actually, I have three."', '"I have heard terrible tales of black rains, ashen fields, and metal that screams. I have consoled myself that the tales were a myth of some fevered mind. But today I saw a walker—and now I fear the truth."\\n—Kasib Ibn Naji, Letters', '"I have suffered a thousand lifetimes of agony on this wretched world. I\'ve far less time to share with you, but I assure you, no less pain."\\n—Ob Nixilis', '"I know just the person for that job."', '"I know to whom I owe the most loyalty, and I see him in the mirror every day."\\n—Starke', '"I lead my horde to the northwest. I won\'t return until the ice wizards fall and their fiendish contraptions are crushed!"', '"I might almost pity my enemies—if it wasn\'t so amusing to watch them die."', '"I once had an entire race killed just to listen to the rattling of their dried bones as I waded through them."\\n—Volrath', '"I stand for every cobbler, tanner, and fool in this town—and they stand for me."', '"I use maps to find out where explorers have already been. Then I go the other way."\\n—Javad Nasrin, Ondu relic hunter', '"I used to joke that he had been exiled for being too smart. Now I know why he never laughed."\\n—Glissa Sunseeker', '"I was born to glory."', '"I watched its blade swing through me, but I was hollow, empty. I saw its face contort in rage but could not hear it snarl."\\n—Klattic, Boros legionnaire', '"I will keep watch."', '"I\'m one masterpiece away from ruling this pathetic world."\\n—Saldrath, master artificer', '"If we cannot live proudly, we die so!"\\n—Eladamri, Lord of Leaves', '"If you hire a sell-sword, you\'d better watch your back. Hire me, and I\'ll watch it for you."', '"In Barrin\'s name!" cried Lyna as Hanna\'s sword passed through her, "Ertai sends word that the portal is open—but not for long!"', '"In ages past, bargains were struck and promises were made. Now we must collect on our debt. Begin the hymns."\\n—Moruul, Khalni druid', '"In desperation, Konda sent warriors to parley with the ogre-magi. No one knows whether they were slaughtered at Shinka or if they even reached its bloodstained walls."\\n—*Observations of the Kami War*', '"In our hands, the natural world finds more beauty than nature alone could ever provide."', '"It is Yawgmoth\'s will incarnate: an efficient machine that replaces inefficient flesh."\\n—Tsabo Tavoc', '"It is all in my grasp. Every petty dream, every grand scheme, every soul, every fear. It all flows through me and from me."\\n—Memnarch', '"It is evidence that some pure corner of the world must still exist."\\n—Djeru, former Tah-crop initiate', '"It is not a goal, but a process—the process of creating the perfect Phyrexia."', '"It\'s gingerbread, like Mother makes. What is there to be afraid of?"', '"It\'s not just what you know. It\'s knowing where to find what you don\'t."', '"It\'s time for the \'Smash, Smash\' song!"', '"Knowledge demands sacrifice."\\n—Tojira, swamp queen', '"Kor armorers buy the scales and claws. Elf oracles buy the rest."\\n—Nablus, North Hada trapper', '"Lay sacrifice to the godsire that it may spare us, but save some for his progeny who also will hunger."\\n—Syeena, elvish godtoucher', '"Let each challenge make you a better warrior."\\n—Anthousa of Setessa', '"Let those idiot priests tremble! A new era in unlife begins here and now. Oglor, raise the lightning vane!"\\n—Stitcher Geralf', '"Lies cannot long withstand the harsh light of day."\\n—Lavinia', '"Life cannot be created and then abandoned. It must be nurtured and fed so that it may express its ripened might."\\n—Freyalise', '"Light passing through a powerstone is refracted by eternity and colored by planar energy. I wonder how the world appeared through Urza\'s eyes?"\\n—Teferi', '"Mana lurks in all things, even in the depths of one\'s own heart."', '"May knowledge be our sanctuary."\\n—Yora, academy researcher', '"May our blessings sever the tongues of the forsaken."\\n—Elesh Norn, Grand Cenobite', '"May you wake to find you were only ever a dream."\\n—Mephidross curse', '"My child grew from rot and ruin, yet she bloomed."\\n—Multani', '"My children will rule over all!"', '"My criticism of the Izzet is that their impulse for learning seems too much like impulse and too little like learning."\\n—Trigori, Azorius senator', '"My favorite part of getting into the infantry was getting out again."\\n—Gerrard of the *Weatherlight*', '"My flesh holds no secrets, monster. The spirit of Mirrodin will fight on."\\n—Vy Covalt, Mirran resistance', '"My master believes anything is achievable."', '"My motive is not vengeance but mercy. I deliver the soulless back to their severed souls."', '"My rule persists beyond death itself."', '"My specialty is theoretical universal limits and ways to circumvent them."', '"No good will come from what you seek. Turn back now or suffer an ignoble death far from your home."', '"No matter how strong, an unarmed fighter is no more than a fool."', '"No one can fight the tide forever."', '"No rest. No mercy. No matter what."\\n—Memorial inscription', '"No, not \'washed\' ashore. It *walked* ashore."\\n—Shafring Hulm, beachcomber', '"Nothin\' beat surprise—\'cept rock."', '"Nothing could ruin such a fine day, Saffi."', '"On dark nights you can still see the light of the Vess girl\'s lantern out in the Caligo, seeking her lost brother. Those who follow are doomed to join her endless search."\\n—"The Fall of the House of Vess"', '"Once I dreamt of death, but now it dreams of me / And only rats and rotting flesh can hear my silent plea."\\n—Mundungu chant', '"Only a knife left for a fortnight in the hollow of a ghastbark tree can inflict a wound so grave."\\n—Kithkin superstition', '"Our border lands fall under the grip of Heidar\'s second winter. Go forth and reclaim them for Yavimaya."\\n—Kaysa, elder druid of the Juniper Order', '"Our noblest thoughts are our very first and our very last."', '"Our people are torn by infighting. Until the two sides reconcile, our laws can carry no meaning."', '"Our revered ancestor Seshiro gave us wisdom greater than poison and fangs."', '"Passions can\'t be shackled by laws or mastered with logic. The choice is freedom or death."\\n—*Volume IV, The Book of Fire*', '"Perfection is at hand. You have been freed of weakness and made *compleat*."\\n—Sheoldred, Whispering One', '"Petals within petals within petals, tadpole. The truth lurks below an opulence of illusion."\\n—Neerdiv, fallowsage', '"Places, everyone!"\\n—Judith', '"Prayer rarely explains."\\n—Orim, Samite healer', '"Preachers of freedom forget that conformity can be beautiful."', '"Reality has exiled me. I am no longer bound by its laws."', '"Seal the furnace vents. Admit no others. We\'ll tend our forges without their tainted ways."\\n—Decree of Urabrask', '"Send your champion. I could use a light workout."', '"Shame to let good gold go to the grave."', '"She will come back to me."', '"So, the survivors from Oxid Ridge are on the move. Let them come and witness predation in its purest form."\\n—Glissa', '"Speak little. Do much."', '"Stand still and try not to look like prey!"\\n—Skerk Hobnett, wilderness guide', '"Stay away from my friends!"', '"Step lightly and we might be able to use it as a bridge."\\n—Ib Halfheart, goblin tactician', '"Take a quiet moment to reflect on your sins."\\n—Cleph, Order of Redeemed Souls', '"Tawnos\'s blueprints were critical to the creation of my armor. As he once sealed himself in steel, I sealed myself in a walking crypt."\\n—Urza', '"The Argivian University taught me two things: always look to the past, and never dismiss what appears useless."\\n—Hanna, *Weatherlight* navigator', '"The Reito Massacre was a testament to the kami\'s unstoppable power. The human defenders might as well have been moths battling a forest fire."\\n—*Great Battles of Kamigawa*', '"The best expedition would be an entire team of me."', '"The best way to teach is by example."', '"The blood of your ancestors ran heavy on this soil. Now it\'s your turn to sacrifice for the glory of Shiv."\\n—Viashino heretic', '"The clashing warriors turned to face O-Kagachi, the greatest kami, and their sigh of awe was their last breath."\\n—*Great Battles of Kamigawa*', '"The dragon has no pretense of compassion, no false mask of civilization—just hunger, heat, and need."\\n—Sarkhan Vol', '"The echo of silence is music to my ears."', '"The elves tend the forest, and the forest sustains the elves. My role is to ensure that the cycle continues."', '"The embers of our homes still smolder, and already the villages of Kjeldor burn in retaliation. What they have started, we will finish."\\n—Lovisa Coldeyes', '"The fools thought me dead. But I built an empire inside my tomb."\\n—Kerrick, sleeper agent', '"The gods here may walk among the people, but they are not with them."\\n—Gideon Jura', '"The hardest thing is finding the right ingredients."', '"The heroes of the past nourish our spirits by their example—and nourish our crops by their decay."\\n—Jeddeg, philosopher of graves', '"The humans and their gods never blessed me. Only the pride deserves my allegiance."', '"The light of my master\'s guidance traverses all boundaries, even those separating life and death."', '"The mist clothes us when we are bare, hides us when we are alone, and unites us when we are together."\\n—Nirit of Pashona\'s band', '"The partisans have unearthed a strange artifact. None know its origin, but it gives them hope of a life beyond."\\n—Elspeth\'s journal', '"The past is buried for good reason."', '"The second mage learned to dissipate blasts of lightning. Threat and response: thus did the study of magic progress."\\n—Naban, dean of iteration', '"The secret entrance should be near."', '"The secrets of Phyrexia are expensive. You will pay in brass and bone, steel and sinew."\\n—Kaervek', '"The snapper is still when all else moves\\nAnd strikes when all are dozing."\\n—*Tales of the Vintara Forest*', '"The spirits of old have not left us unguarded."\\n—Uros, Pendelhaven elder', '"The treasures of the ancients belong in museums, not in the grubby hands of grave robbers."', '"The unfathomable is upon us, students. I have no doubt you will rise to the occasion."', '"The war sent Kamigawa into turmoil. Here it was spring and there winter. For some, time stood still, while for others, moments flashed past like minnows in a pond."\\n—*Observations of the Kami War*', '"The white fox grinned. \'How about a bet, dragon? If I win, the skies are mine.\' After he stopped laughing, the dragon agreed."\\n—*Tales of the Fae*', '"The wind whispers, \'come home,\' but I cannot."\\n—Teferi', '"The world is a puzzle, and the mind is its key."', '"There are terrors lurking in the unseen corners of us all."\\n—Crovax', '"There are times when destiny calls forth a people and demands an action. *Now* is the time. *We* are the people. *This* is our action. Charge!"\\n—Eladamri, Lord of Leaves', '"There is always more to give."', '"There is great wisdom in rushing headlong into combat . . . if you\'re prepared."\\n—Kenjek, captain of the Thousand Swords', '"There\'s always room for improvement."', '"These fiends are slightly less tolerable than you."\\n"A sentiment that warms my heart, sister."', '"These guards are the most disciplined military unit in the city. They couldn\'t fight their way out of a broom closet, but they\'ve got discipline."\\n—Gerrard, to Sisay', '"They can\'t feel pain. They just wiggle \'cause they\'re scared."', '"They\'re not worth much, but they\'re easy to catch."', '"They\'re still here?! The cockroach may have finally met its match."\\n—Teferi', '"Think of this new life not as a gift from the angels but as a command to fight for their cause once more."\\n—War blessing of Serra', '"This close to Rimewind Keep, no avalanche is nature\'s doing."\\n—Ukoten, centaur chieftain', '"This god held prisoner in human hands has put all humanity in the hands of angry gods."\\n—Masako the Humorless', '"This will work," Gerrard called to the elves as he used the forge to strengthen the aboroth, "but if it doesn\'t, we won\'t survive to care."', '"Those who can\'t survive are of no consequence."\\n—Tsabo Tavoc', '"Though their ideals are leagues apart, Urza\'s and Mishra\'s creations have a surprising harmony with one another."\\n—Tocasia, journal entry', '"Thoughtweft binds us together as one, part of an intricate pattern that would unravel if even one thread came loose."', '"Time and space are just new battlefields to be mastered."', '"To my sword I owe my glory, but to my shield I owe my life."\\n—Sarlena, paladin of the Northern Verge', '"To prevent, one must first predict."', '"To those who can hear it, Gaea\'s battle song brings power as swift as sunlight and as enduring as the deep roots of the forest."\\n—Gamelen, Citanul elder', '"Today\'s paperweight, tomorrow\'s leveler."\\n—Bruenna, Neurok leader', '"Tonight we\'ll eat a farewell feast. Cold corn porridge is not enough. / Let\'s peel papayas, pineapples, and mangoes, drink coconut milk, / and bake bananas."\\n—"Love Song of Night and Day"', '"Torahn gore these shifty fishtails! You can\'t even get close to one."\\n—Tahngarth of the *Weatherlight*', '"Touch no tree, break no branch, and speak only the question you wish answered."\\n—Von Yomm, elder druid, to her initiates', '"Unskin these impure bodies, Great Yawgmoth, that the flesh may welcome your blessings."\\n—*Phyrexian Scriptures*', '"Until my last breath, I will defend the realm."', '"Until this expedition is done, that blade is your guardian, your liberator, and your best friend all rolled into one."\\n—Yon Basrel, Oran-Rief survivalist', '"Vulshok flail, Viridian shield, loxodon blade . . . Tazzir, bring the Moriok hook and assemble the rookies."\\n—Vy Covalt, Neurok agent', '"Warmth. Safety. A fully-stocked larder. You\'ll find nothing like Edgewall Keep in the wilds, I promise you that!"', '"Watch over my father. Tell him I\'m safe, but I won\'t come home until I find out how to bring him back to his senses, and Kamigawa is again at peace."\\n—Michiko Konda, last letter to General Takeno', '"We have faced horrors of war and terrors beyond imagining. We will overcome the uncertainties of this new life."', '"We have fought this far and lost too much. We will not turn back."\\n—Grizzlegom', '"We often bury our pasts, and then someone comes along and digs them up."\\n—Gerrard of the *Weatherlight*', '"We pray to Avacyn on high. On snow-white wings fearless you fly. Keep safe our souls. Keep safe our lives. May angels watch us from the skies."\\n—Children\'s prayer', '"We thought the clouds had moved from the night sky. Then the night sky moved, and the horizon grew wings."\\n—Josuri', '"What do you have that I cannot obtain?"\\n—Mairsil, the Pretender', '"What fire forged, fire remembers."', '"What was heads again?"\\n—Mercadian magistrate', '"What was once formed by masons, shaped by smiths, or given life by mages, I will return to the embrace of the earth."', '"When we\'re aloft, I love to lean over the *Weatherlight*\'s railing and watch the patterns the griffins\' shadows make on the clouds below."\\n—Sisay, Captain of the *Weatherlight*', '"Whichever side wins, I\'m sure the banquet will be superb."', '"Who will be the hero of my tale?"', '"Why, Gideon? Of all people, why save me?"', '"With a diet of hydras, giants, and massive serpents, anything would get that big."\\n—Corisande, Setessan hunter', '"With this crown, assert your authority."\\n—Crown inscription', '"Wood is wasted in the dirt."\\n—Orcish proverb', '"Yawgmoth\'s corpse is a wound in the universe. His foul blood seeps out, infecting the land with his final curse."\\n—Lord Windgrace', '"You and your ship will make a fine addition to my fleet."', '"You are wrong," Volrath said. "I do not hate the living. They often prove quite useful to me." And then he laughed.', '"You can build a perfect machine out of imperfect parts."\\n—Urza', '"You can\'t hope to comprehend the plans that are in motion."\\n—Tezzeret', '"You cannot fight the storm."', '"You may enter the city—once the toll is paid."', '"You wish to remember this lesson? I will write it down for you."\\n—Senifet, vizier of Bontu', '"You\'d almost think Volrath doesn\'t want me here."\\n—Gerrard', '"Your enemies may be cowardly, my lord, but one should never call them gutless."', '"Your life is finished, your name lost, and your work forgotten. It is as though Mazeura never existed."\\n—*Chainer\'s Torment*', '"Your life will set with the sun."', 'A barricade only buys time. So the wealthy buy more barricades.', 'A blazing sun that never sets.', "A foul, metallic stench clogged Urza's senses. It was then he knew his brother was no more.", 'A king in Jund, a serf in Esper.', 'A mark of unity when you want one; a fierce guardian when you need one.', 'A ray of hope breaks through the shroud of rain.', 'A savage cry with the power to shatter minds.', 'A sickness stirs in its eyes, a nightmare born in darkened wails.', 'A sojourn through time gave dark inspiration to one gifted young mind.', 'A tried-and-true favorite of many wizards, whatever their school.', 'A typical day for a giant. A momentous event for a goat.', "A weapon of evil, redeemed in Gideon's hand.", "Aboard her ship, the *Dragon's Smile*, Kari follows no one's rules but her own.", 'After encountering them, Squee finally lost his appetite for bugs.', "Ages ago, a party of elves took cover to let one pass. They're still waiting.", "Akros's greatest heroes are also its royalty.", 'All Auriok children know the tale, "Bolgri and the Long Day of Squashing."', 'All crave the Blessed Sleep. Few receive it.', "All the world is Purphoros's anvil.", 'All who listen hear their own song, a unique melody played just for them.', 'Altered by Phyrexian science, corrupted by black mana, and twisted by rage, Ertai still looked in the mirror and saw only glory.', 'An army of squirrels is still an army.', 'As Gideon kept the brood lineages at bay, Chandra incinerated the bound Eldrazi titans.', 'As Jhoira restored the *Weatherlight*, a mushroom growing in its hold unexpectedly became her first crew member.', 'As insubstantial, and as powerful, as the wind that carries it.', "As long as it's never left empty, this magic pouch produces coins every dawn.", 'As renegade forces closed in on the Aether Spire, Consulate blockades failed one by one.', "As the Phyrexian contagion corroded Karn's body, the praetors whispered psalms to corrupt his mind.", 'As the flames engulfed her, Chandra opened her heart and offered up her greatest regrets to be consumed by the inferno.', "As the shadow of the Mephidross spread over the Tangle, the vampires' territory expanded.", 'At his side, humble beasts become weapons more deadly than sharpened steel.', 'Battle tempers soldiers as fire tempers steel.', 'Because the dead have no will to resist.', 'Before labs or lectures, there was insight.', 'Being one would be an honor, if the word "honor" had any meaning in Phyrexia.', 'Beware the generosity of demons.', 'Blood is thicker than mortar.', 'Both forge and pyre.', 'Bred as living shields, these slivers have proven unruly—they know they cannot be caught.', "Centuries ago, a pyromancer's spark ignited a fiery conflagration.", "Changelings can't remember where they came from. They just know it wasn't a cradle.", 'Chaos does not choose its enemies.', 'Crippling fear precedes it. A foul stench accompanies it. Death follows in its wake.', 'Death greeted the world with a roar of desert air.', 'Designed by Brian Fargo', 'Designed by George Fan', 'Do not be so caught up in keeping track of time that you forget to make use of it.', "Doing something at the last minute isn't so bad when you can make that minute last.", "Dominaria's most ancient evil.", "Don't underestimate the aerodynamic qualities of the common goblin.", "Dromoka's followers forsake blood ties so that they may join a greater family.", 'Dwarves may teach at the speed of stone, but their results are solid.', "Dweldian magi don't enter the Realm of Thrones when they die. Instead their souls are drawn to great works of magic.", 'Each eye sees a different possibility for tomorrow.', "Each of Malakir's great families boasts a contingent of nulls appropriate to its rank in society.", 'Each temple is a door to a horrible future.', 'Each time the saw blade bit, the tree spat it out.', "Entry 434: There's more to Avacyn's madness . . .", 'Even an enemy is a valuable resource.', 'Even as humans regained the upper hand, some still willingly traded their lives for a chance at immortality.', 'Even baloths fear its feeding time.', 'Even the greatest hero begins with nothing.', "Even the oppressive cold of the cave could not temper Eladamri's ire.", 'Even the trivial can inspire.', 'Every life ends, but life itself never does.', 'Few things are truly "lost" at sea.', 'Few who encounter the strange, human-like grove leave once the lilting chorus of the dryads reaches their ears.', 'For his family, Barrin made a funeral pyre of Tolaria.', 'For hundreds of years Ugin slept, encased in the cocoon of stone and magic Sarkhan had created using a shard of a Zendikari hedron. As Ugin lay dormant, his spectral guardians kept vigil.', 'Forged out of flowstone for the queen of Vesuva.', 'Fortunately for it, Mirrodin is a plane without salt.', 'From a marvel of magical mechanization to a smoking stack of scrap in one easy step.', 'From concept to paper to reality.', "From deep in the caves beneath the forest, the hierophants planned the druids' raids against the enemy.", 'Gaea forged her soldiers into self-wielding weapons that struck down all impurities.', 'Gerrard studied the globe as Mirri kept watch. Suddenly, his eyes widened. "This is Dominaria!"', 'Greenweaver Mina and her twin brother Denn lead the last of the Mul Daya into an uncertain future.', 'Grieve for the soul in death dishonored.\\n—Shadow Guild saying', 'He bids his minions rise from their graves to their knees.', 'He wants to watch Ravnica burn, one soul at a time.', 'He was born of the Mirari, thrust out of his homeland before he was even aware. Left without purpose or meaning, he found both in the pits.', "He's boss because he's smart enough to get out of the way.", "He's set to compete in every race at the Fair, and he plans to win them all.", 'Her centuries-long search is ended.', 'Her poppets bring joy to the truly depraved.', 'Her warriors are the last defense against the coming storm.', 'Hidetsugu held over a dozen oni in blood oath. At his touch, rocks scorched. At his word, cities burned.', 'Hidetsugu never relinquished a grudge. He let it burn within him, gathering ever greater intensity until the final moment of vengeance.', 'His family was the first to reach out to the human monks. He soon knew as many koans as he did blade strikes.', 'His marvels of artifice pale in comparison to the developing machinery of his mind.', 'His mind whirled with grand plans, never thinking of what might happen if he were to succeed.', 'His roots reach deep, nurtured not by soil and rain, but by millennia of experience.', 'His spark lost, he plots revenge upon the plane whose corrupting mana fractured his soul.', 'Hours after the Helvault opened, his powers returned twice as strong as before.', "Hurkyl's research at the College of Lat-Nam wasn't enough to stop the two brothers, but for centuries thereafter her spellcraft taught artificers restraint.", 'I cast a thousand tiny suns—\\nBeware my many dawns.', 'If a land can be said to have a heart, Okina is the heart of Kamigawa.', "If it can't be had here, it can't be had on any world.", 'If it comes for you, die boldly or die swiftly—for die you will.', 'If the eyes are windows to the soul, their souls are not of this world.', 'If your flesh can withstand the flame, the spirit of the dragon will burn within your soul.', 'Illusion steals reality from the unwise.', 'Immolation is the sincerest form of flattery.', 'In an age of war, time is measured not by sand but by blood.', 'In times of madness, people cling to the familiar, monstrous though it may be.', 'In war, as in society, position is everything.', 'In war, the best leaders are open to all tactics.', 'Infinite possibilities contained in a finite space.', 'It *is* the thing that goes bump in the night.', 'It descended on Estwald like a sudden storm. Moments later, only ashes and agony remained.', 'It harnesses the power of night in a land where daylight fears to show itself.', "It has witnessed history's most significant events, one incarnation after another.", "It is everywhere you've ever been.", 'It is the forest beyond the horizon, the mountain waiting to be climbed, the new land across the endless sea.', 'It provides what every discerning mage requires—time to think.', 'It sees shaped stone and carved wood as mutilations.', 'It stalks the Regathan highlands, leaving behind melted snow, scorched earth, and the charred corpses of would-be temple robbers.', 'It strikes at your soul, heedless of your prayers.', "It's easy to believe you're a god when you're twice as powerful as everyone else.", "It's not always gold the thief is after.", "It's the favored mount of military commanders as well as anyone with a flair for the dramatic.", 'Its mood changes with the weather, and vice versa.', "Its plow wasn't designed for snow, but to carve a path through shrieking armies.", 'Its scars cut deeper than its blade.', 'Jace awoke to the certainty that he was lost.', 'Jariad burned the midnight oil, burned through scroll after scroll, and then burned down his laboratory.', 'Karn and Hanna stood over the recovered Legacy artifacts like loving parents over sleeping children.', 'Karn said nothing—he just grasped the powerstone and squeezed tightly. The wild flashing ceased.', 'Kavu leaders instinctively protect their herds from harm.', 'Knives in the sky, cries in the air, and blood on the ground.', 'Kuldotha, wellspring of molten metal, temple of the goblin horde.', 'Land charred black, rivers boiled, Crops and wells alike despoiled, Mountains leveled, forests felled— Footprints of the beasts of Keld.', 'Lightweight, flexible, and protective.', 'Like the price of goods, the value of the routes was renegotiated daily.', 'Living metal encasing dying flesh.', "Made from trout scales and crawfish whiskers, merrows' shimmering banners flash in the water like lightning.", 'Many hands for many evils.', 'Merrow schools rarely form by design. They come together naturally as eager learners surround the wisest teachers.', "Mirrodin's creator still lives, still shapes metal, and still commands world-shaking power.", 'Mood: A friendship that can outlast death.', 'Mother, sleep / Dream our lives Our roots your soul / Our leaves your bed.', "Never before have there been so many brilliant minds and wondrous inventions in one place. Denizens from every corner of Kaladesh will flock to the once-in-a-lifetime Inventors' Fair.", 'No matter where you find them, goblins love rocks.', "No mortal could atone for Ihsan's betrayal. Redemption required him to become something else.", 'No one is as dedicated to perfection as a stitcher working on their latest masterpiece.', 'No part goes to waste.', "Not all elves embrace the pastoral life. Some still roam the forest's edge, forever making war against their hated enemies.", 'Not every tale ends in glory.', 'Nowhere on Ikoria are monsters more integral to the landscape than Ketria, where the river itself will stand up and roar.', "Oketra's closest viziers are known as her chosen, though others may have a better claim to that moniker.", 'Olka collected the evening mist for years, studying its secrets. Once she learned its essence, she could vanish with a thought.', 'On Fiora, no matter is settled until King Brago offers an opinion.', "Once a fierce foe, she would become one of Madara's greatest protectors.", 'Once a vision of constancy in the sky, the moon had long been hidden from view by the haze that chokes the heavens. The very sight of it had become a sign that change was in the air.', 'One shard of Selenia yet remained.', 'Only in mirrors do heroes find their equal.', 'Ordinary moths follow it, drawn to its light.', "Paradoxically, to tilt the massive jug for a sip, you'd need the energy of the giant's tonic.", 'Perfect for getting through to the consuls.', "Phyrexia had tried to take Urza's soul. He was relieved that Shiv tried to claim only his soles.", 'Phyrexian or Mirran, most goblins stick to the job they know best.', 'Plague and death wrapped in one convenient package.', 'Plan for victory, or prepare for defeat.', 'Poets dream the verses of otherworldly stories. Artificers dream the blueprints of otherplanar artifacts.', 'Predators try to separate the young, old, or injured from the rest of the herd. The alternative is crushing defeat.', 'Radiant\'s eyes flashed. "Go, then," the angel spat at Serra, "and leave this world to those who truly care."', 'Remade by Eldrazi magic, Tuktuk inspired an entire clan of misguided goblins.', "Reminders of Memnarch's reign still skirr across Mirrodin, reminiscent of his form if not his power.", 'Seeking the company of plants ensures that your wits will go to seed.', "Sentries guard Ravnica's landmarks and outlying districts, unaware of these places' import to the maze.", 'Sharpen your ears\\n—Elvish expression meaning "grow wiser"', "She doesn't escort the dead to the afterlife, but instead raises them to fight and die again.", "She is the apex of the artificer's craft, the spirit of the divine called out of base metal.", 'She provides marks of protection to those she chooses as family.', "She remembers every word spoken, from the hero's oath to the baby's cry.", 'Silent as a snowdrift. Inexorable as an avalanche.', "Since the war began, the castle's walls mark the only place on Kamigawa where no kami has ever set foot.", "Skybridges from across Kylem converge at the grand stadium of Valor's Reach.", 'Some emeritus professors return from their wanderings periodically to share tales of the mystical wonders of Arcavios.', 'Some mages forsake their scrolls and libraries to learn at the feet of ancient trees and sacred stones.', 'Some think that dryads are the dreams of trees.', 'Sometimes quantity, in the absence of quality, is good enough.', 'Sometimes the *eludha* is a sacred harmony of souls. Sometimes the bonder grabs some fur and holds on tight.', 'Sometimes you go to hell, and sometimes hell comes to you.', 'Sorin has gathered grudges for centuries, patiently awaiting the day he can exact the perfect vengeance.', 'Squee: "What\'s that?" Ertai: "It\'s a magical book." Squee: "Am I smart enough ta use it?" Ertai: "You could say that."', 'Step 1: Find your cousin. Step 2: Get your cousin in the cannon. Step 3: Find another cousin.', 'Students at the Dekatia Academy learn that being sent to study with her is a lesson in itself.', 'Suffer the little creatures, for they may yet rise up and beat you senseless.', 'Survival itself is no small reward.', 'Syr Branigan always remembered to kiss his good luck charm, having lost his foot to wolverines the last time he forgot.', 'Taj-Nar, throne of Raksha Golden Cub, destined leader of the leonin prides.', 'Tarek could not tell whether he was losing his blood or his mind.', "Tel-Jilad, sanctum of the ancient trolls, keepers of the secret of Mirrodin's origin.", 'The Arbiter is a conduit of justice, a will so disciplined that it dispenses justice without ego or remorse.', "The Aurora transformed Nibb and Gyik from mischief-makers into feral marauders. They still don't know much about tool safety.", 'The Cabal never expected its creations to create servants of their own.', "The Cho-Arrim didn't rely only on a secret location to protect their Fountain.", "The Extinguisher's curse lasted long after her departure.", 'The Izzet quickly suspended their policy of lifetime guarantees.', 'The Kalonian word for "ammunition" is the same as the word for "bait."', 'The Quicksilver Sea hissed and bubbled at the indignity. The Vulshok shaman just smiled.', 'The Soul of the World has returned.', 'The Thran learned to capture mana, but power inevitably escapes its bonds.', 'The accusations spread like hungry flames.', 'The air was filled with the cracks and snaps of flesh hardening as the new sliver joined the battle.', 'The ancient green dragon Claugiyliamatar is often seen with a mangled corpse dangling from her mouth.', 'The armies paused, silent, as the warriors reflected on the sunsets of their youth.', 'The blades of a Sultai assassin stab like the fangs of a dragon.', "The book shrieks horribly until its cover is opened, granting the spirit inside a moment's rest from the painful stirrings of the book's contents.", 'The bright tunnel sometimes leads back to life.', "The cat warriors recognized this Jedit's face, but not his fierce loyalty to Efrava.", 'The competition is but one aspect of the spectacle.', "The cube's surface is pockmarked with jagged runes that seem to shift when unobserved.", 'The earth walks, strongest of all.', "The earth's memory is long, its retribution brief.", 'The emotional echoes of dryad gatherings attract lost souls.', 'The first to arrive on Dominaria from their distant home, the marids are the oldest tribe of djinn and the most respected by storm and sea.', 'The flow of time was disrupted; like a flooding river it rose from its banks. Tolaria was drowned in an instant that stretched toward infinity.', 'The forest rose to the battle, not to save the people but to save itself.', 'The gatekeepers are so fastidious that even the winds must wait to pass.', 'The glow from within looks inviting, but woe awaits whomever finds out who stokes the fire or what simmers in the pot.', 'The goblins have forty-two different words for "ow."', 'The heart of Ravnica disappeared before anyone could strike a blow in its defense.', 'The heart of a golem gives life to more than just the iron husk around it.', "The helix was the finest example of Mishra's campaign strategy: if he couldn't have Argoth, no one could.", 'The infamous Ezuri commands the highest bounty the vedalken have ever placed upon an outlaw.', 'The investigator felt a pinch on his ankle. When he looked down, something glittered in the sand.', 'The knights see a mighty quarry. The dragon sees breakfast, lunch, and dinner.', 'The light of the rising star empowers the champions of tomorrow.', 'The locks on the cages of the damned are opened with keys of marrow, sinew, and blood.', 'The mind is a beautiful bounty encased in an annoying bone container.', "The mine's riches never end, nor do the moans of the spirits doomed to haunt them.", 'The model incorporated the fifth sun effortlessly, as if it had always known.', 'The more victims he kills, the more likely he is to get the right one.', "The more you pay for the lesson, the better you'll remember it.", 'The most nimble of creatures, it chases the most sacred luminence.', 'The musical sound of its turning triggers the tumblers of revelation.', 'The persistence to overcome obstacles is the most esteemed of kor virtues.', 'The price of prophecy is a vacant eye socket.', 'The priests plead for your anguish and pray for your despair.', "The renegades mounted an aether disruptor aboard a lightweight thopter to destroy Tezzeret's Planar Bridge.", 'The rifted multiverse became a sea of conflicting realities, each peopled by possible versions of every living being.', 'The rumors are horrifying; the truth is worse.', 'The sky split, and the air crackled and roiled. The Phyrexian invasion of Dominaria had finally begun.', "The sparkmage shrieked, calling on the rage of the storms of his youth. To his surprise, the sky responded with a fierce energy he'd never thought to see again.", 'The spell fell upon the crowd like a dragon, ancient and full of death.', 'The squabble over succession was quickly replaced by the struggle to survive.', 'The storm rages and the earth breaks.', 'The thief doubled back twice, doused herself with perfume, crossed the ocean, and still woke up with her pursuer close on her heels.', 'The thunder of its hooves beats dreams into despair.', 'The vines overgrew the construct, snapping gears and soaking up aether.', 'The wafting smells are both scrumptious and suspicious.', 'The wisest man builds his house *behind* the rock.', 'Their flesh is as sodden as the fens in which they live, oozing to fill any wound and squishing to absorb any blow.', 'There are no "weak" creatures on Jund. Even the smallest can strike a deadly blow.', 'There is no glory to be gained in the kingdom of the dead.\\n—Vec tomb inscription', 'There is no loftier ambition than the pursuit of knowledge.', "There's lots of time like the present.", 'They charge into battle and out for their morning walk with the same exuberance.', 'They stay on the battlefield only long enough to consume the losers.', "They're fun to train—if you like stubborn, aggressive, and fiercely territorial.", 'Things buried on Innistrad rarely seem to stay that way.', 'This secret society of mages manipulates the beliefs and opinions of others.', 'Those who expect betrayal at every turn are seldom disappointed.', 'Those who hear her go mad with inspiration.', 'Those who lead others to wisdom become the wisest themselves.', 'Those with knowledge are wise to listen to those with imagination.', 'Though Volrath is long dead, the slivers have become everything he wanted them to be: mindless instruments of destruction and despair.', 'Though its mind has long since rotted away, it wields a sword with deadly skill.', 'Though the Time of Ice has ended, its relics still slumber in New Argive.', 'Tidal forces of the blood moon wrench and buckle the land, drawing monoliths of stone and soil toward the flaming orb.', 'Titania rewards all who honor the forest by making them a living part of it.', 'To bear the shield of the pariah is the highest honor a Boros can receive—and the last.', 'To protect the alliance between Kjeldor and Yavimaya, they trained in the ways of both.', 'To save Dominaria, nine planeswalkers sought the annihilation of Phyrexia itself.', 'To the sorrow of all, its rage became focused on those who once stoked it.', 'To the sorrow of all, its winds found sin in the hearts of those who once learned from its wisdom.', 'Transformed at his own wedding, he promptly ate the banquet, the gifts, and the guests.', 'Trod on by a gargadon\\n—Kipamu expression meaning "wiped out"', 'True power is achieved through blood and sweat. But mostly blood.', "Under the master's eye, skills are honed sharper and spells cut deeper.", "Unlike most churches, at Orzhova it's best to pray before you arrive.", 'Urza convinced many Dominarians not only to set aside their differences, but to embrace them.', "Vela snuffs out every trace of Krond's reign, leaving pure nightfall in her wake.", "Verick held his breath. Breathing wouldn't reveal his position, but it would force him to smell the goblins.", 'What once soared high above Tarkir is now reduced to a seat.', 'What some see as "distracted" is really "fathoming the unfathomable."', 'When Lorthos emerges from his deepwater realm, the tides bow to his will and the coastline cowers in his presence.', "When Worzel summoned Segovian angels to fight Thomil's Gargantikari gnats, the ensuing battle numbered among the Multiverse's least destructive.", 'When a changeling adopts a form no other changeling has taken, a rune appears in the caverns of Velis Vel to mark the event.', "When he's holding the hammers, everything looks like a nail.", 'When it awoke, it shattered the hillsides to make way for its passage.', 'When it awoke, it spawned nameless thousands to herald its arrival.', 'When it awoke, the worms of the earth hissed in a chorus of beckoning.', 'When its power is threatened, the council speaks with a unified voice.', 'When the Mirran resistance arrived, the furnace dwellers looked to Urabrask for guidance. His decree stunned the others: "Let them be."', 'When the earth shudders, the sky overflows.', "When the rebels couldn't breach the castle to kill Lalor the Obstinate, they tried a more internal approach to depose the pretender king.", 'When the smell of passing thoughts piques its hunger, its maw becomes primed with acid and a taste for brains.', 'While the realm has laws, in the wilds there are other ways of balancing power.', 'With an explosion that shook the foundation of the city, the *Weatherlight* burst from the underground hangar.', 'With every end, a new beginning.', "With heavy heart, Urza doused one world's light to rekindle another's.", 'With such great footsteps, everything is within walking distance.', "Wizards fought over the stone to exploit its power. Goblins fight over it because it's shiny.", 'Wreckage from the Phyrexian Invasion provided the rats with a seemingly unlimited number of breeding grounds.', 'Xenagos reveled while Theros burned.', 'Your father has no horns!\\nYour mother wears a bell!\\nYou drink the milk of goats!\\n—Talruum taunts']
